{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1049458-ic-awakening-2e-to-the-strongest","id":1049458,"title":"[IC] [Awakening 2E] To the Strongest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T13:49:29-08:00","id":1049458,"title":"[IC] [Awakening 2E] To the Strongest","content":"<i><b>Hibis, Upper Egypt, 14th year of Alexander, Aquarius rising</b></i><br /> <br /> There are two parts to Egypt. The Black Land, Kemet, is the thin long ribbon of fertile soil along the banks of the Nile. The Red Land is the desert, the domain of Set, nothing but endless rocky sand and storms and scavengers, inimical to life. The Red Land defies order, a maddening expanse of shifting dunes with nothing to support human life but the desperate hope of an oasis and/or divine intervention. Even Alexander could no more rule the desert than he could rule Ocean.<br /> <br /> You're going into the Red Land.<br /> <br /> Even with all your charms and spellcraft, it took more than 10 days to get here with a trade caravan departing from Waset, which the Hellenes now call Thebes. You've gone west from the Nile, the direction the dead go. There are five main oases in the western desert, and you've come to the one furthest south, the Kharga Oasis. This distant eye of the Black Land in the middle of the Red is called <b>Hibis.</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Like this, but more populated and less destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/4/3355/3263125855_6eccebf194_z.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/4/3355/3263125855_6eccebf194_z.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/4/3355/3263125855_6eccebf194_z.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://c2.staticflickr.com/4/3355/3263125855_6eccebf194_z.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://looklex.com/e.o/slides/kharga03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://looklex.com/e.o/slides/kharga03.jpg</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Let me paint you a picture: <b>Hibis </b>is a walled and garrisoned mud-brick town, about one square kilometer, in the center of a green ring of fields irrigated by the shallow blue canals of the carefully-managed oasis. Overlooking the town from the north is the <b>Temple</b>, which you understand is dedicated primarily to the Theban Triad (Ammun, Mut, and Khonsu) but honors many gods a traveler might need to pay respects to, emphasis on <i>pay. </i>East of town is a <b>Camp </b>of tents set up by passing traders and nomadic desert tribes, raucous and dirty and much cheaper than staying in town. Hibis is an outpost on the &quot;40 Day Road,&quot; a desert trade route that moves gold, spices, rare animals, slave labor, etc between the Kushite city of Meroe (legendarily skilled metalworkers and international traders, proudly unconquered by Persia or Alexander) to the south and the city of Asyut in Upper Egypt. Lots of transients and traders and scammers and men driven mad by the desert sun.<br /> <br /> The five of you, plus the half-Wise Kemsit and the wolf-spirit Urbi, are gathered in a large tent, sharing a final meal with the caravan that took you here before you enter town. The sun will be setting soon. It sounds like you can buy private lodging at a house in town for the next few days (Availability **), but don't stay too long. Your patron, Ratri, has asked you to go here as the first leg of a much more treacherous journey into the Red Land to investigate a Mystery, a rare astrological convergence that can best be observed from a long-forgotten ruin which she saw in a dream.<br /> <br /> You can go over the details later. For now, you have a few minutes to sit and get your bearings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:28:41-08:00","id":1049491,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribe</a> of Anpu</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12 (3)</div> </div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Enjoying the company of their host at this last meal, he raise his glass <b><span style=\"color:darkred\">&quot;I salute you and wish wellness upon you and yours, may the rest of your journey find peace&quot;</span></b> with that he takes a drink. <b><span style=\"color:darkred\">&quot;Will you be leaving in the morning or remaining for a few days.&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> He continues to pick at the dates and meats. He is looking forward to the walk in the cool of the evening just him and Kesmit under the stars. The town can wait for there is nothing more exhilarating than a cool evening and the company of a beautiful woman. having spent more than just a passing moment in this thought he forces his mind to return to the company within the tent.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-16-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:38:36-08:00","id":1049613,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> <br /> He had a bad feeling about this trip. It was quite some time since their Patron last sent them all together, and this time she was sketchy on the details, even by her standards. Still sitting on the ground, he reaches out for a date. <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;So... this is where we part ways. Perhaps we will meet again on the road, but for now our path takes us elsewhere. Now if you excuse me, I will once more go over our supplies, see if there's anything we need to pick up in town tomorrow. Gentlemen&quot;</span></b> - he nods to his Awakened companions - <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>meet me under the palm tree before we go rest, would you?&quot;</b></span> He means the tree they had passed a few minutes before setting up camp.<br /> <br /> He goes outside of the tent and to the carts, creating a mental shopping list if there is anything missing. He will visit the nearby Camp tomorrow morning, see if the locals can tell him anything about the area or the ruins in the dream. He goes over every detail she gave them about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 02-16-2017, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T20:00:11-08:00","id":1049664,"title":"","content":"The caravan master and his party aren't staying in Hibis long. They'll restock tomorrow, deliver wheat to the temple, take on any more cargo or passengers, and head south not long after. No one understands the value of time like a merchant.<br /> <br /> Kesmit is obviously bored to tears of your current company, and very much looking forward to some privacy and fresh air with her husband. She's worldly, but a week of desert travel with a bunch of traders is about her limit. At least there should be some excitement soon.<br /> <br /> As Alketas is leaving the tent, a meaty hand claps him on the shoulder. &quot;Halt, soldier! You're not leaving without one last round of senet, are you? I almost won last time!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's another traveler from Thebes in the caravan, a thick and affable Corinthian veteran by the name of Talaus, bit of a rowdy drinker, who fancies himself an adventurer and latched onto Unbound and Prism as fellow soldiers. He picked up a garishly painted senet board and pieces for an ungodly price off one of the traders, and he's been eager to get some use out of it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unbound can do his &quot;games of strategy&quot; oblation if he's willing to spend an hour matching wits with a Falstaff type. Roll Gnosis+Composure and regain that many Mana.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:50:15-08:00","id":1049932,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;Oh, of course. The ropes and saddles will wait, won't they?&quot;</b></span> He says, turning to Talaus and dressing in one of his friendly smiles <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;Let's find a quiet spot and play. See you later, comrades.&quot;</b></span> - he says to his companions.<br /> <br /> As they go and prepare the board and pieces, Unbound studies the other soldier's figure, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/486781\" target=\"_blank\">looking</a> for signs of ill intent, like restless gaze or sweaty hands. He didn't trust this man - after all, a slightly goofy, affable outside is a classic cover for a much more mischievous inside. <br /> <br /> Focusing his mind on the game and feeling the refreshing effect it had on him, Unbound looks around, studying the faces of the people he is about to travel with, especially Strife's wife. He was confident about the rest, but as far as he knew she didn't have the advantage of magic nor the skills to survive in the wilderness. Still, if her husband thought she would make it, then he won't rush his judgment. As the game continues, he tries to make a casual conversation with his partner: what's his story? Where is he headed? What does he hope to find?*<br /> <br /> <br /> [OOC]<br /> (<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/486793\" target=\"_blank\">Oblation roll</a>. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/486796\" target=\"_blank\">10 again</a>)<br /> <br /> *Unless he actually knows these things already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:53:17-08:00","id":1049969,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribe</a> of Anpu</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12 (3)</div><hr /><br /> <br /> As the conversation hit a lull he thought it would be a good time to take down the Momentary names of those that were parting ways, it would only take a moment and then he could be off with his wife. Quietly leaning into into Kesmit <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Just a few moments and then we can escape this crowded tent&quot;</b></span> grabbing his ink and papyrus he starts to draw the symbol of each person present, including his own.<br /> <br /> When he finishes he stands and takes Kesmits hand <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Thank you for the evening and I shall bid you all goodnight. We shall secure lodging then go for our walk, if anyone should need us.&quot;</b></span> with that he leads his wife from the tent and towards Hibis in search of lodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:41:07-08:00","id":1050000,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 8/15</div><br /> Strictly speaking, this journey had been far longer than necessary. From the high places his eyes stretched many parasang and in such fashion he and his could pass where they would. Yet he did not begrudge the delay, for it had given him many nights in which to measure the slight differences in the place of the stars and perform the calculations of their influences.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">I echo the sentiments of my traveling companion. Your have been more than hospitable to us and I shall not forget it. I do wonder if I might not impose on you one final time. I had meant to leave an offering in the temple of Meroe in the hopes that such yazata as smile so favorably upon them might likewise be gracious to me. Would it be too great an imposition for you to carry a small offering for me and leave it with the priests when you arrive?</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:00:27-08:00","id":1050228,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Antikatoprismos: </b><b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Obrimos Gnostikon of the Arcadian Mysteries</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Health: OOOOOOO </b></span>| <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> Antikatoprismos kepts mostly to himself, periodically sketching the sights they've seen - but it was all of the same which he had already seen. Instead, he addresses the Strife. &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">Indeed. I will go with you, if you do not mind - I have a wish to stretch my legs after traveling on those blasted animals for so long.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:41:03-08:00","id":1050259,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribe</a> of Anpu</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12 (3)</div><hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;You are welcome to walk into Hibis with us to secure your lodging, and there should be plenty for you to do while we are on our walk. Anyone else care to stretch their legs.&quot;</b></span> Gathering up his papyrus and ink and securing it in a satchel he will give a nod to their host <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Once again I thank you for your hospitailty.&quot;</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T22:10:59-08:00","id":1050322,"title":"","content":"<b>Unbound</b><br /> <br /> Talaus isn't deep enough for any hidden malevolence below the surface. You have an eye for these things, and his Cruelty doesn't go any further than a soldier's relative comfort with killing and a tendency to view non-Hellenic cultures as fun games to play rather than people. He laughs and curses and spits easily, and doesn't seem too bothered by wasting money. He knows nothing of sorcery.<br /> <br /> You've gotten bits of his story during the long journey, but he's happy to go over it again. He's in his late 30s, a farmer's son from Corinth, joined Alexander's army after originally being drafted by his city to fight against him, went on campaign as far as the Hydaspes. He's got an elaborate and sound effect-filled story about fighting a war elephant, solo, with nothing but a broken arrow and a jar of wine. He promised he would return home and build a shrine to Hestia if she let him live. Went all the way back to Hellas with Alexander two years ago, took an arrow in a siege, deliriously offered to serve Hermes as a wandering adventurer instead if <i>he </i>would let him live. Hermes came through in the clinch, so now his patron god is the Messenger. Talaus has a very practical relationship with the divine. He's been wandering in Egypt for a while as a bodyguard and gambler, and after &quot;a little bit of trouble&quot; in Thebes, he's headed south of the border to Kush for a while. They make swords there that can cut elephants in two! That'll be something to hang on the mantle of his mansion one day, won't it? For now, he's thinking he'll stay in Hibis for a few days before he hitches a ride with another caravan. He's got a poorly-defined &quot;bad feeling&quot; about this group, and his gut hasn't led him astray yet.<br /> <br /> As for Strife's wife: she's no Amazon, but she must be able to take care of herself if she's made it this far. Herodotus was shocked by the independence and tenacity of Egyptian women compared to Hellenes, so maybe Strife knows something you don't. Still, he might want to consider leaving her in Hibis during the expedition. As you understand it, she can carry his magic without being physically present.<br /> <br /> Talaus has enough skill to provide a reasonable challenge. Senet is a game of strategy that represents the journey of the soul through the afterlife against many dangers, although Talaus is convinced that it's basically a war game. While he chatters, your meditation on the challenge refreshes your spirit.<br /> <br /> <i>(Regain 3 Mana.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah</b><br /> <br /> The caravan master, a tall thin man with a colorful cloak called Paneb, is not particularly devout. But you've been so gracious that he's willing to accept your parting gift. He promises to bring whatever you like to the priests in Meroe. They expect to get there in about 20 days.<br /> <br /> <b>Strife and Antikatoprismos</b><br /> <br /> You study the present state and direction of the other travelers in the caravan, and record the runic hieroglyphs of their Names. You might want to use wax tablets for Momentary Names, like folk magicians do for charms- you can more easily melt the wax and reuse the tablet when the Momentary Name's usefulness ends. The traders have been wary around you, since it's obvious that you're a priest and know the secret of the written word. You perceive a whole world of texts and inscriptions that is utterly mysterious to most of them.<br /> <br /> <i>(Technically it costs 1 Mana to record a Name, but I won't worry about it right now.)</i><br /> <br /> The three of you leave the tent and head through the fields toward Hibis. Women and men are still planting among the sprouts, since the growing season hasn't ended quite yet. The temple looms on the hill north of town, with its series of gates and sphinx-lined avenue facing the east.<br /> <br /> You pass through the guarded gate of the walled town. The sentries are watching the camp of traders and nomads, but not very closely. Threat level: green-yellow. Most Egyptians, at least in Lower Egypt, are tight with Hellenic culture and view Alexander as a liberator from the Persians. He's much less popular in Thebes, and some believe it might grow into a center of dissent. It remains to be seen whether Hibis feels safe under Hellenic rule, or whether they just don't really care who's in charge along the Nile as long as the food keeps coming.<br /> <br /> Kesmit is a bit better at talking to the locals than you two, so she asks around, and pretty soon she's found an amateur innkeeper named Nefer who rents out the second story of her and her husband's house to travelers. It looks like you'll be able to secure the place and sanctify a room as a ritual space, as long as you're not screaming incantations or summoning demons or anything. For three silver drachmas a night, you can have the space and a square meal for as long as you like.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Renting a place for your Safe Place and Sanctum merits is Availability **. I assume you're gonna do this, and I'll move along.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <br /> By nightfall, you've all gathered in a bedroom upstairs at Nefer's. Kesmit is setting up the ritual accessories (she's real good at this stuff), Urbi is lounging. You have time to plan.<br /> <br /> Ratri sent you all a message in dreams last month. Apparently she (or one of her informants) had a &quot;god-dream&quot;, an oracular vision. There will be a rare astrological convergence during the rising of Aquarius (IE, this month) which can best be observed from a site in the deep southern desert of Upper Egypt. She called this place the <b>Hand of U'mat</b>, but as far as she knows, it hasn't appeared on any map since before the first Pharaohs. The most she could give you was a vision of the place, rising like a mirage out of the wasteland: three thin palm trees, a broken black stele, and something like a great stone hand trying to reach out of its grave. The stars and planets are aligned overhead in a very specific pattern around the Milky Way, or Hathor's Milk, or Tiamat's Tail, or whatever you prefer.<br /> <br /> She knows that <i>something </i>significant will happen during the convergence, some cosmic Mystery, but she couldn't say exactly <i>what. </i>She described a <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">fallen star</span> crashing to earth, the Hand of U'mat opening to accept a gift, possibly a gateway to the hall of some lost god. But she's adamant that the convergence lasts for just one night, and only happens once in a dozen lifetimes. Ratri has asked you to recover whatever you find, and if at all possible, bring it to her in person when she next visits Lower Egypt in a few weeks. At the very least, she asks you to witness the convergence and bring word of what you saw.<br /> <br /> So, to recap: you don't know where you're going, when you need to be there, or what you'll find. This is the price of patronage. But you're sorcerers, and one astronomer, so you've got options.<br /> <br /> What you are <i>not </i>is survivalists or desert nomads. Actually<i> finding</i> the Hand of U'mat will involve many days of searching for a needle in a constantly-shifting wasteland, based on nothing more than a dream vision and a general direction. Even if you tied your Fate to reaching the Hand eventually, you still have to actually navigate the Red Land to get there. How are you planning to do that?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alright, there's your hook. It's currently Night 1 of Aquarius, and sometime between now and Night 28 is the convergence. Finding the Hand will be a once/day extended action, but with you guys' Skills, you'll need a lot of mundane or magical help, and that's going to take precious time. I'll just present some mundane options for simplicity's sake.<br /> <br /> I suggest you start by rolling Intelligence+Survival or Ride to come up with a list of likely dangers and the equipment you'll need to overcome them. Anyone with at least 1 dot in those Skills can roll.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, Day 2, you can go out to seek more information and/or acquire stuff. Manipulation+Streetwise to talk to the traders and nomads in the Camp for advice would be good. Imhotep could use Contacts (Bureaucracy) to talk to the working scribes at the Temple. Khvarenah could roll Intelligence+Science (Astronomy) to narrow down exactly what night the convergence should happen: penalty if done on Nefer's roof, bonus if he gains access to the Temple. And you have the benefits of Sanctum back at Nefer's place.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T03:46:47-08:00","id":1050410,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribe</a> of Anpu</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12 (3)</div> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;</b></span></span><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>If it was a place of power then it still may be and we should look for the lay lines that lead to such places. I could view these lines and call upon the hands of Fate to guide us through the web. This will set us upon the right course.&quot; </b></span>He starts to take mental note of what it will require to follow the strands of fate to lead them to their destination. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Once in the area we could consult those long dead for their guidance to the Hand.&quot;</b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T05:12:10-08:00","id":1050435,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12<br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;All due respect to the powers of the Moirai, how can we be sure these ley lines won't lead us straight in the paths of brigands, wild animals, even sandstorms?&quot;</b></span> Not waiting for the answer, he continues <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;And if nothing else, none of us will survive in the desert for long by ourselves, Fate or no Fate. If there are no objections, I will head to town tomorrow morning, see what the latest word around is and try to learn of the dangers ahead. If nothing else, I am sure there is no shortage of guides who can be... persuaded to cooperate. As Strife says, under the sands lie countless ghosts - and spirits - who just need a little coaxing to get us where we need.&quot;</b></span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:13:31-08:00","id":1050475,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Antikatoprismos: </b><b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Obrimos Gnostikon of the Arcadian Mysteries</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Health: OOOOOOO </b></span>| <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> OOC: I would've liked to ask Talaus what he knows about the swords of Kush - new metallurgical techniques are fascinating.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I have no objections. We have enough coinage between ourselves to hire the very best - both in the forms of guides and supplies. &quot; </span></b>He purses his lips and thinks about it. <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Another option is that we are not operating under a veil of secrecy. Perhaps we can simply ask some of the locals whether they know of this stone hand?</span></b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T18:06:17-08:00","id":1050825,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> none | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 8/15</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">Before we go from this place and begin our diverse activities, prudence moves me to advise that I secure the favor of my holy namesake for each of us. If you wish to partake of such blessing, I will seek it when we are done conversing. In the vein of </span><span style=\"color:#00008B\">practical concerns, I mean to gain access to the temple to make use of their star charts. It is my hope this will allow me to determine when this convergence is to occur and perhaps to assist us in determining its location. Should I fail in that I can likely still estimate the time of the event from here.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Persian turned toward the window, toward the light as was proper of a devotee of Mazdayasna and chanted the true words, recalling as he did the sky beyond the sky he had glimpsed. With a final invocation, he held his star-measuring staff aloft and waved it over the company.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008b\">May we be one with all the righteous. May we be one with all the virtuous. May brightness increase and continuance be the reward of the offerer. May they who are deserving of it be here mentioned. On those of them who set their hope on us have I here thought. Let their good deeds, honest offerings, and Mazda be here remembered.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Quick and Dirty Casting<br /> Exceptional Luck: 4 free reach, 1 for 8-again, 2 for affect spellcasting, 1 for instant cast<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487304\" target=\"_blank\">5 Succeses</a> - Exceptional<br /> Note: made a mistake. Actually 5 successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Casting Exceptional Luck rote to give us all the Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast conditions<br /> Instant, Sensory, Advanced Duration, Advanced Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -6, Duration -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Order Skill +6, High Speech +2, Shadowname +2, Order Tool +1<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 + Arche 4 + Yantras 11 - Penalties 8 = 12. Casting roll.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487305\" target=\"_blank\">6 Successes</a> - Exceptional<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-18-2017, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:23:56-08:00","id":1051233,"title":"","content":"Khvarenah invokes a blessing on the group, altering their Fate in a more beneficial direction. Everyone feels the breath of magic in their vicinity in their own way. Once you get an idea of the challenges facing you for desert travel, you can make some headway tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Everyone has Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast. These Conditions last for the next day. The first time your character resolves a magically-granted Condition in a scene, they take an Arcane Beat. You can also receive a regular Beat for resolving a mundane Condition once per scene. Remember we're using Group Beats, so just note when you would gain a Beat and I'll keep a running tally.<br /> <br /> Khvarenah regains 2 Pneuma for his 2 exceptional spellcasting successes. I'll think of better/more specific rewards in the future.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-19-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:10:30-08:00","id":1051256,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool),<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</span></span></div> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Feeling the magic of a much stronger Fate will-worker wash over him he feels truly blessed. There is much he can learn from Khvarenah and perhaps some day he will get that chance, but for now that must wait. He must find a place to meditate and for the he needs to find where they bury their dead. Standing he kisses Kesmit </span><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;I need to go for now, I will return in a while.&quot;</b></span></span> Then he exits the room.<br /> <br /> Once downstairs he will ask Neref for directions to the temple </span><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Would you be so kind as to provide directions to the temple, I must prey.&quot;</b></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The dead usually buried near a temple he should be able to find it easily enough. After receiving directions he will and once outside he will walk towards the temple at a leisurely pace taking in the town as he goes. Once he nears the market he decides to stroll through to see if he can find something that catches his eye.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-18-2017, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T09:40:10-08:00","id":1051553,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/11 (2)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 7/15</div><br /> <br /> <br /> He smiles at the other scolar's suggestion. <span style=\"color:#40D080\">&quot;Let us try asking tomorrow. Right now, we require finding out what we need. In fact, here's my suggestion (Urbi, you can contribute, too)...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> -----<br /> Rolling to assist Prism, resolving Informed: Int 3 + Ride 1 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487689\" target=\"_blank\">4d10h8, 2 successes</a><br /> Rolling to assist Prism: Power 3 + Rank 2 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487691\" target=\"_blank\">5d10h8, 7 successes</a>. By the Gods, Urbi knows some things about the Red Land","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T11:05:37-08:00","id":1051581,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We'll resolve this roll first. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12852\" data-vbnamecard=\"12852\">Silver_Smoulder</a> can roll Int+Survival with +2 from Imhotep and +7 from Urbi. For the exceptional successes, Imhotep takes <b>Team Player </b>and Prism takes <b>Desert-Wise</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Team Player</b><br /> You are inspired to work well with others.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Resolve this Condition when supporting a teamwork action. You may spend Willpower to add +3 dice to the primary actor's dicepool rather than yours.<br /> <br /> <b>Desert-Wise</b><br /> You have insight into navigating the Red Land.While this Condition is active, any extended actions to navigate or find sustenance in the Red Land in which you are a supporting or primary actor may make 1 additional roll, above and beyond what the Attribute+Skill would normally allow.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Reach your destination in the Red Land or abandon your search.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:15:44-08:00","id":1051788,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 10/15<br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</span></span></div> <br /> After the others went about their business the Persian found a quiet corner and took out a tablet of glazed and fired clay, tiny ordered rows of cuneiform filled both sides. He ran his fingers over them feeling the sharp edges as he remembered when he wrote them. It had been a gift in recognition of the completion of his training, though finding someone else literate to do the writing would have multiplied the price many times. He remembered Adarbad making a great spectacle of the surprising him when it was finished, even though he had handled it more than the brickmaker. The memory brought a smile. In many ways these smiles were the true gift, and <i>they</i> did come as a surprise.<br /> <br /> He left the house heading up and east. It was late, but the priests would have watched the place of the sun's rising, counting the days until the rains. He let the light guide him, following the glinting of sunlight on dew or the shaft of sunlight between buildings. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Shifting the Odds to pick up Allies (local priesthood) Resolving Inspired for Exceptional Success on 3.<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency, +1 to find the Ally within the hour.<br /> Reach: 3 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency -6, Duration (primary) -0 (3 steps free), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: whatever +1, something +2<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Shadow Name 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1 + Sacrement 1 - Penalties 6 = 9.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487861\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes - Exceptional</a><br /> <br /> Casting Serendipity Rote to cause Academics to be suitable for situations I find myself in.<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency, +2 to substitute any skill<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -8 (3 steps free), Duration -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: whatever +1, something +2<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Academics (order skill) 6 + Shadow Name 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1 - Penalties 10 = 10<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487876\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:14:46-08:00","id":1051993,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> What follows is a string of actions built on presuption that a) nothing of note happens between them and b)everything works exactly as I think it does. If you want to resolve it differently, be my guest.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Seeing as some of his companions already started searching for equipment or even doing magic, Unbound decided that he, too, will spend what's left of the day meaningfully. He donned his cloak and as he exited form the house, he said <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm going to do some mingling among the locals, see if they know something of the road ahead. Maybe they will even draw us a map.&quot;</span></b> Grinning, he entered the sandy alleys of Hibis and turned to the Camp, determined to find the place where all of the local merchants, caravaneers and ne'er-do-wells gathered.*<br /> <br /> Knowing that he needs to remain discreet in such company, he concentrated on remaining entirely forgettable. The plan was simple: eavesdrop on whatever rumors about the Red Land or the mysterious place from the dream circulated around here. Then, he would find someone (the owner, most likely, although he was aware of other possibilities) who could tell him more on their basis or at least point out to someone who could have a map of the region or at least knew it well enough to describe it to him. In every detail. To that end, he planned to use the mightiest tool at his disposal: a lie. With a little help of magic, perhaps...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;Good evening, sir! I wonder if we could talk about the Red Land for a while. You know, I am in a hurry, but I will send word that you helped me to my friends, and in a week's time a messenger will leave you a bag full of coins, solid gold! What? What do you mean: why I would go into the Red Land? Maybe I have a death wish, surely you have greater concerns than some stranger's fate, like that reward coming your way.&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> *<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> i.e. an inn, or whatever passes for it in rural Egypt at the time. If there's more than one such place, he tries to visit all of them and finally stops at the largest one.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488060\" target=\"_blank\">Lying to the innkeeper</a> - a failure, resolving Steadfast condition to turn it into a single success<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488043\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Incognito Presence (Resolving Inspired to get exceptional success on 3 successes)<br /> Instant, Self, Advanced Duration (1 hour), Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency -0, Duration (primary), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech, Order Tool, Sacrament<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + High Speech 2 + Order Tool 1 + Sacrament 1 = 10<br /> (the effect of an exceptional success would be that I gain the Inspired Condition again, if you allow)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488071\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Emotional Urging to relax the innkeeper<br /> Standard Time, Sensory, Advanced Duration (1 scene), Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency -0, Duration (primary), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech, Order Tool, Sacrament<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + High Speech 2 + Order Tool 1 + Sacrament 1 = 10<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488070\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> First Impressions to boost the first impression to Excellent<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration (1 scene), Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency -4, Duration (primary), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech, Order Tool, Sacrament<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + High Speech 2 + Order Tool 1 + Sacrament 1 - Penalty 4 = 6<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 02-20-2017, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:21:20-08:00","id":1052065,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Antikatoprismos: </b><b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Obrimos Gnostikon of the Arcadian Mysteries</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast, Desert-Wise| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Health: OOOOOOO </b></span>| <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12<br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Well, let me consider the following...&quot; </span>as the Obrimos tries to figure something out about the desert, through the magic of his allies.<br /> <br /> OOC:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488111\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488111\" target=\"_blank\"> Dice Roller &bull; Orokos.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488111\" target=\"_blank\"> http://orokos.com/roll/488111 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Orokos is a tool site for role-playing games, such as Dungeons and Dragons 4th edition, allowing players to upload characters from Wizards of the Coast's Character Builder program and providing a dice roller and attribute calculator. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:02:32-08:00","id":1052246,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>Night 1</u></i><br /> <br /> Antikatoprismos</b> and <b>Imhotep</b>, experienced travelers that they are, compare notes about the fundamentals of long-term desert travel. They prepare a simple shopping list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Desert Travel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locating the Hand of U'mat will be an extended Stamina+Survival roll, one roll per day. You don't know the target number. The primary actor, which will be one of the PCs, can make a number of rolls equal to their Stamina+Survival rating, while the dicepool itself is modified with bonuses and penalties. Other PCs can contribute as secondary actors with Wits+Survival or Manipulation+Ride, scouting ahead or preparing food and shelter or guarding against weather conditions.<br /> <br /> At the bare minimum, you will need to rent some camels and bring enough water and rations for a prolonged trip. (no bonus, Availability 2)<br /> Instead, you could ask the desert nomads for their better-trained camels. (+2 bonus to primary actor and supporting Ride rolls, Availability 3)<br /> It would be wise to find a skilled guide who knows the desert. (Allows up to 2 additional rolls, but must find and convince someone. Availability ?)<br /> <br /> The Red Land is an Extreme Environment, but its level varies over time. It's always at least Level 1 from heat or cold, and it can reach Level 2 on hot days or cold nights. On dangerous days (not nights), it can reach Level 3 from heat and wind. If you're caught in a sandstorm (Set forbid), it's Level 4, and mundane Survival gear won't protect you. Extreme Environments are explained on Mage 224. Much, but not all of this can be mitigated with Forces.<br /> <br /> Basic Survival gear (protective clothing and canvas tents) gives a +1 bonus to Survival rolls and downgrades the Environment level by 1. (Availability 1 to outfit the group)<br /> Instead, Advanced Survival gear (desert nomad clothing, tents, and advice) gives a +2 bonus to Survival rolls and downgrades the Environment level by 2. (Availability 3 to outfit the group)<br /> <br /> You can choose to travel by day or by night. The weather is more extreme by day, but it's dark and there are more potential predators by night. Minor bites and stings can be deadly serious in the wasteland.<br /> <br /> If you're planning to travel by night, or just want an easy source of fire, you could buy torches and fuel. (Counters 2 dice of Poor Light penalties, Availability 1)<br /> The body's natural healing is more difficult in the desert, but if you bring bandages and salves, you can treat injury. (Enables Medicine rolls, Availability 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>Urbi, the friendly possessed jackal, has some more thoughts: &quot;Good news is, we've got a safety net. Lord Anpu's gift of Pathfinding should always point me toward our target if I have a moment to commune with Him. But if the Hand is magically hidden or warded, which it probably is, it doesn't always work so good.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Strife </b>strolls through town. It's mostly mud-brick homes and barracks and warehouses, some of them two or three stories. Nefer just laughed and pointed outside when you asked for directions to the temple- it looms on a hill overlooking the town, so it's easy enough to find. On the way, you pass through the market that fills one of the narrow streets. The best finds (for merchants and householders, anyway) were picked over this morning, but a few things catch your eye:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Market Goods</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Javelin (2L damage, Strength 2, Size 2, range 10/40/80. Availability 1 for as many as you want.)<br /> Torch (Counters 2 dice of Poor Light penalties, Size 1. Availability 1 for as many as you want.)<br /> Myrrh (+2 to Socialize rolls, great gift for Kesmit. Availability 2 for a jar.)<br /> <br /> Many stalls are selling simple charms to wear around the neck or wrist, absolutely none of which trigger your magical senses.<br /> <br /> No one at the market is willing to serve as a guide, and they try to dissuade you from going into the desert at all. It's too dangerous, even for a priest!</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Khvarenah </b>works a bit of magic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Shifting the Odds gets an extra Potency for the x-success. You've got Allies (Hibis Priesthood) 5 for the remainder of the Aquarius rising, IE, the next month. You can ask for up to 5 dots' worth of favors total this chapter, and after that it starts requiring a roll.<br /> <br /> Serendipity lasts until Night 2, affects up to 8 rolls. Remember that you need to specify a goal that Serendipity is helping you reach, although it's clear enough in this case.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Strife </b>and <b>Khvarenah </b>arrive at the Hibis Temple together, serendipitously enough, as the sun is setting behind the stone complex. The temple overlooks a glittering pool made from redirecting the oasis. It's contained behind stone walls of its own in multiple layers: the sanctuary of the idols is in the deepest center, but also the priests' quarters, the library, the granaries. There are various levels of security and ritual purity to get deeper inside successive archways.<br /> <br /> As you two approach the avenue of lion-headed sphinxes outside, two of the lower scribe-priests (well-fed men with shaved heads and white robes) are having an animated discussion just inside the little courtyard of the first archway. One of them looks over at Khvarenah and smiles, like you've just proved his point. &quot;Speak of a Persian and he will appear! You look like an educated man, and you, sir, are clearly a fellow priest. Come in here, help us settle this. Is it true or false that we can calculate the exact day on which the planets will again be in perfect alignment, as they were at the world's creation?&quot;<br /> <br /> The speaker introduces himself as Mitry. He really hits it off with you two, especially Khvarenah. He's a highly educated dilettante, maybe a little too big for this pond, and he's overjoyed to meet someone both intelligent and worldly. He's willing to help you out with whatever you need and spread the word with his boss that you're good people- the scribes would love to talk shop with an outsider for once. Of course you'll need to ritually purify yourself before you can enter the temple buildings, but they can make that happen.<br /> <br /> Strife notices something weird while Khvarenah is chatting. There's a dark stain, like dried blood, at the base of one of the sphinxes lining the avenue. Once he sees the blemish, he can't ignore it, like a bit of meat stuck to a speaker's lips. Why hasn't it been washed away yet? Do the priests not see it? It would be rude to say their temple is dirty, but still, it's unsettling.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Medicine-3 if one of you wants to look closer at the stain. Serendipity applies for Khvarenah.<br /> <br /> Tell me what you want to to do at the Temple, I'll tell you if it requires an Allies favor and when you can do it.<br /> <br /> Also, you guys are at the bottom left: <a href=\"http://jeanclaudegolvin.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/egypte-hibis-temple-vue-generale.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://jeanclaudegolvin.com/wp-conte...e-generale.jpg</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Unbound </b>dons his cloak and disappears in the desert town, Obi-Wan style.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Incognito Presence takes effect for the next hour, and you get Inspired related to this task.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The encampment south of town is around a dozen colorful tents and yurts with camels tied up nearby, drinking from the oasis. The farmers (and guards) aren't letting the nomads and ne'er-do-wells who hang out here come anywhere near the crops. Some of the tents and saddlebags are dyed and even embroidered with patterns representing, you assume, clan and tribal loyalties.<br /> <br /> One of the camels, a perfectly mundane one tied to a post and chewing weeds, has something embroidered on its nearly empty saddlebags: a stylized image of a snake, coiled around a jackal, eating its own tail. The exact sigil of the sorcerer who tried to murder you. Weird. I'm sure it's nothing.<br /> <br /> Most of the action is a firepit that travelers and adventurous locals are gathered around, joking and chattering and chewing khat and playing flute horribly. You lurk for a while and pick up talk.<ul><li>Nile-based traders passing through the Red Land between cities in Egypt or Kush stick to routes defined by familiar landmarks and sometimes guard encampments, they don't really &quot;explore.&quot; Some are hoping that Hellenic rule will institute better patrols along the trade routes, like back when the old Dynasties had the strength to do that. It sounds like bandit activity has mostly been reduced since the Hellenes kicked the Persians out, which makes the recent robberies and killings by one particularly vicious band stand out more. [Your old friends, maybe?]</li> <li>Nomadic tribesmen interpret the Red Land as a collection of oases with relatively safe routes between each of them, like a storm with many eyes. They follow greater or lesser travel cycles between the oases, which is how they mark both distance and time. They talk about going &quot;shallow&quot; or &quot;deep&quot; into the Red Land, a measurement that is related to but distinct from how many oases you stop at (drink from?) during a journey. A long journey can be shallow, and a short journey can be deep. [Int+Occult-2 to interpret this.]</li> <li>Unlike the trading caravans, the tribesmen don't particularly venerate the gods of the Nile. They do show respect to Set and a lesser god called Ha, both of whom are represented at the Temple. A few of them quietly mention a divinity called Sin that lives deep in the Red Land, presumably a tribal patron god. [You can roll Int+Academics to make sense of all that god talk, or ask someone else.]</li> <li>Some of the traders swear they've seen one of the sha, the beasts of Set (in the way that a common jackal like Urbi is the beast of Anubis), padding alongside their caravan. The other traders are highly skeptical. [You can roll Int+Animal Ken to interpet this.]</li> </ul><br /> After asking around for a while, whispering in peoples' ears and quickly being forgotten, you find a half-drunk woman from town who seems to know all the regulars. She's about to push you away when you offer money, but through Fate's blessing, she takes a swig of wine first and decides to give you a chance.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Here's how I'll represent this a little abstractly. It's going to be a Social Maneuvering action to find a high quality guide, which your Impression level applies to. You only need to worry about Impressions with social maneuvering, not the majority of instant social rolls. You might deal with multiple people at the camp, but ultimately the action is Unbound trying to get closer to the guide.<br /> <br /> The camp has 5 Doors and starts at Average impression. The woman who knows everyone doesn't have very high Composure, so both of your spells overcome her Withstand. You open 1 Door with Emotional Urging, and raise her impression to Excellent, so you can make one roll per hour. I'll count your lying-Steadfast roll for that, which opens a second Door.<br /> <br /> Because you promised plenty of gold and made it known that you're rich and eccentric, you have the camp's attention (satisfied their Vice). You're now at a base level of 3 Doors and a Good impression, so you can roll again once per day starting tomorrow. Hopefully that all made sense.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After you chat for a while, she brings over a bearded nomad with missing teeth, who's drunk enough not to notice that he couldn't see you a minute ago. The woman says: &quot;This guy's from Clan Ibex, they'll do <i>anything. </i>Even crazy stuff,for crazy <i>hic </i>rich Greeks! You need to find him here tomorrow night, okay? He'll get you what you need!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Try to wrap up what you're doing tonight, you'll have more chances in the coming days. Time limiting what you can do per day is a big factor in this scenario.<br /> <br /> The pot has 3 Arcane Beats right now.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:58:34-08:00","id":1052458,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b></div></span><div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 5/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Cratfing Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool),<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div><hr /><br /> Market:<br /> He will take a back sheath and as many Javelins as will fit in the sheath. He will take 1 Jar of the Myrrh. He will tell the merchant that he will be by in the morning to pick up the Javelins but he will take the Myrrh with him.<br /> <br /> Temple:<br /> Arriving at the Temple , coincidentally with Khvarenah, and walking into the first alcove he sees the two men talking. Paying his pleasantries to the two of then and listening to their question he is about to answer them when he sees the blood. At that point he will spend one point of Hekau and activate his Mage Sight for Death, Fate and Matter, along with the Level 2 Utility attainment Eyes of the Dead. Also activating his legacy attainment to look at the souls of the two in front of them. Looking around the area before inspecting the blood. He has never been a subtle man and after looking at the two men's souls and looking around the area with his Mage Sight he will drop the Mage Sight if there is nothing that catches his eye. If everything is in place he will walk over towards the blood and knee down, touching the spot he will ask <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;What happened here?&quot;</b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:59:44-08:00","id":1052638,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Antikatoprismos: </b><b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Obrimos Gnostikon of the Arcadian Mysteries</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast, Desert-Wise| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Health: OOOOOOO </b></span>| <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> Antikatoprismos considers the options laid before the group.<span style=\"color:#800080\"> &quot;To be perfectly honest, I see no reason to limit ourselves to paltry substance, or some blind idiot to lead us through the desert. While I do not wish for a procession with elephants, comely Nubian slavegirls, and scented oils massaged into me every night; I should imagine that we should spend coinage on the very best of guides and equipment.&quot; </span>He draws his bag of gemstones and assorted coinage. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I am willing to go &quot;all in&quot; on this, if necessary.&quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:29:47-08:00","id":1052779,"title":"","content":"<b>Strife </b>sees no ghosts lurking around the temple, no errant <i>ba </i>from a mistreated corpse. He studies the souls of the two priests and sees that both of them are Sleepers who perceive nothing of magic.<br /> <br /> Through Matter, he sees that the temple is much more solid than the buildings in town. Stone, not mud brick. The sphinxes and walls are hardly worn. This place is relatively new, it must have been built during the Persian occupation, rather than the Dynasties. There can't be much old magic here, and what use is magic that isn't old?<br /> <br /> Through Fate, he sees that Khvarenah has tangled these two priests in the web of his own destiny. The entire priesthood at Hibis has been drawn into his orbit like stars following the planets.<br /> <br /> Through Death, he sees...nothing in particular. Everyone here has their soul in its proper place, all five parts in harmony. Still, his palms itch.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Roll Gnosis+Death for a Clash of Wills, as you're aware that something here is hiding from you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mitry doesn't crouch down next to him, which would be beneath his dignity. But he looks over Strife's shoulder and hums. He's surprised, but not at all concerned. &quot;Huh. I never noticed that. It's probably nothing. You know, it's getting late...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:37:01-08:00","id":1052786,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Cratfing Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool),<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> he will spend a point of willpower and the inspired condition<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488549\" target=\"_blank\">Clash of Wills</a>: <u>9d10h8</u> <b>3</b><br /> <br /> Edit 3 successes on the roll, If you can get an exceptional success on a clash of will I did it. I resolved the Inspire so i get a Beat (either an Arcane Beat or a Regular one not sure) and a point of willpower for resolving the beat.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Haggle spend i will power and roll 3 dice. If I fail I will resolve steadfast<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488565\" target=\"_blank\">Haggle</a>: <u>3d10h8</u> <b>1</b> = Success<br /> <br /> I still have the steadfast and down 1 willpower<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-21-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:42:57-08:00","id":1052789,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Satisfied with todays findings and convinced that he won't be able to squeeze out more from the locals that night, Unbound returns to the house where the group is staying, Tomorrow, however, he hoped to find the guide the woman was speaking about, and although he was a little worried about that &quot;craziness&quot; she mentioned, he decided that it's still better than nothing.<br /> <br /> What really got him worried was that he couldn't possibly make any deeper sense of what he has heard at the fire. However, he will share these pieces of information with his more academic companions. Or if they don't know, perhaps the goetic entity within him will, at least about the mysterious symbol from the saddlebags. While again at the camp, perhaps an opportunity arises to investigate it further.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if there is someone else willing to listen to his findings at the house, he will brainstorm it with them. If not, well, it was a long day, one worthy of a few hours of sleep.</div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:50:21-08:00","id":1052799,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You get an Arcane beat (because the Condition came from a spell) and your Willpower point back, yeah. Take this Condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated</b><br /> You've been exposed to a Mystery, and now you're hungry for its secrets. Take +2 on any Scrutiny and Revelation rolls for the Mystery in question.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Fully reduce the Mystery's Opacity.<br /> <br /> The mark has Opacity 3 if you want to Reveal or Scrutinize it (Mage 92). If you do Scrutiny, declare how many Hekau you want to spend (if any) before you roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Strife's knowledge of Death is great enough to push through the veil. He didn't notice the mystical properties of the dark stain because it was intentionally hidden. He can see the priest looking at the blemish, narrowing his eyes, but immediately forgetting why it was important. The mark has a heavy shadow, but understanding why will require looking closer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:55:10-08:00","id":1052802,"title":"","content":"Antikatoprismos looks to Unbound. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;What have you uncovered,&quot;</span> he inquires politely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:58:51-08:00","id":1052806,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 10/15<br /> </div><div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</span></span></div><br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">It is a providence! Just such an errand brings me here, though far less lofty I am afraid. It is indeed possible, provided that you know both the initial positions and have taken proper measurements of the length of their motions. Once that is done it becomes a simple matter of determining the common multiple of all relevant durations. For myself, there is an alignment of particular significance set to occur, the date of which I had hoped to fix more firmly. Might you permit me to study your records and make use of your star watching apparatus?</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:08:40-08:00","id":1052811,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Death/Fate/Matter Mage Sight | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b>LrOOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 7/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Cratfing Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool),<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Before making the roll I will scour my pattern for mana, giving me 8 mana, I will make 6 rolls (if needed) at 8 dice (3 Gnosis + 3 Death + 2 illuminated) with 1 mana spent per roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488555\" target=\"_blank\">Scrutinize 1</a>: <u>8d10h8</u> <b>6</b> = 7 successes - Exceptional Success (3 to lower it to 2 Opacity, 2 to lower it to 1 Opacity, 1 to lower it to 0 Opacity)<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488556\" target=\"_blank\">Revelation</a>: <u>8d10h8</u> <b>3</b> = 3 success. Revealed.<br /> Roll 3 = Not Needed<br /> Roll 4 = Not Needed<br /> Roll 5 = Not Needed<br /> Roll 6 = Not Needed<br /> <br /> Spent 1 mana after all is done. so I actually gained mana due to the scouring. 1 Resistant Lethal wound.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-21-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:53:09-08:00","id":1052862,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">FYI, I'll be playing Unbound as an NPC for a few days while <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10396_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10396\" data-vbnamecard=\"10396\">Woland</a> is out.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Back at the house, <b>Prism </b>(and anyone else) gets the scoop on his fellow soldier's trip to the camp in search of a guide. He's found a lead: a certain group of nomads called Clan Ibex might have a willing and skilled guide for a trip like this, but it will take some searching and convincing to find someone trustworthy. If left to his own devices, he'll be able to find someone by Night 4, but it could be sooner if another mage comes along to help.<br /> <br /> He also passes along some rumors that the others can try to interpret:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Nile-based traders passing through the Red Land between cities in Egypt or Kush stick to routes defined by familiar landmarks and sometimes guard encampments, they don't really &quot;explore.&quot; Some are hoping that Hellenic rule will institute better patrols along the trade routes, like back when the old Dynasties had the strength to do that. It sounds like bandit activity has mostly been reduced since the Hellenes kicked the Persians out, which makes the recent robberies and killings by one particularly vicious band stand out more. [Int+Streetwise-1]</li> <li>Nomadic tribesmen interpret the Red Land as a collection of oases with relatively safe routes between each of them, like a storm with many eyes. They follow greater or lesser travel cycles between the oases, which is how they mark both distance and time. They talk about going &quot;shallow&quot; or &quot;deep&quot; into the Red Land, a measurement that is related to but distinct from how many oases you stop at (drink from?) during a journey. A long journey can be shallow, and a short journey can be deep. [Int+Occult-2 to interpret this.]</li> <li>Unlike the trading caravans, the tribesmen don't particularly venerate the gods of the Nile. They do show respect to Set and a lesser god called Ha, both of whom are represented at the Temple. A few of them quietly mention a divinity called Sin that lives deep in the Red Land, presumably a tribal patron god. [You can roll Int+Academics to make sense of all that god talk, or ask someone else.]</li> <li>Some of the traders swear they've seen one of the sha, the beasts of Set (in the way that a common jackal like Urbi is the beast of Anubis), padding alongside their caravan. The other traders are highly skeptical. [You can roll Int+Animal Ken+1, or Int+Occult-2, to interpet this.]</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><b>Khvarenah </b>gets a good reception, although Mitry's colleague is wary about letting a Persian access a secure location and state secrets.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They're willing to let you into the inner courtyard tonight as an Allies 2 favor and let you make some preliminary measurements under their supervision. But you'll need to make a roll (presumably Manipulation+Academics) at a -3 penalty to convince them you're innocuous, failure means trouble and distrust of you as a spy. Determining the proper dates will be an extended action, target number 10. You can roll once per night.<br /> <br /> In addition or instead of that, you can use an Allies 3 favor to come back tomorrow, be ritually purified for a few hours during the day, and have mostly-private access to their star charts and records during the night, as well as better equipment.<br /> <br /> Either of those is considered a new Allies 2 or 3 favor for each night that you do it, which means you may have to roll (per Mage 105) after a while.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Strife </b>learns quite a lot from viewing the stained sphinx through the eyes of Anpu.<br /> <br /> This is the dried blood of someone whose soul has been overpowered by their <i>sheut. </i>Their shadow has poisoned their own body, mixing with their blood like beer in the veins of a drunk. In your sorcerous sight, you can see the shadows darken around the bloodstain, like the borehole of a worm in rotten wood. The influence of the <i>sheut </i>hides the bloodstain from the unwary, but those with a connection to Death can see the vile graffiti clearly. The outcome resembles the Veiling practice, although the cause is different. The blood has been on this sphinx for <i>decades, </i>maybe as long as a century. Maybe it's some kind of calling card or territory mark. Whoever made this bloodstain, they were more mystically potent than you, but not overwhelmingly so. It's not Awakened magic, there's no Nimbus, but the shadowy blood has an aura of regal, contented fullness, like a sated beast lounging in its darkened lair.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You resolve Illuminated, but you've already received your Arcane beat this scene from a magical condition.<br /> <br /> You can go ahead and assume you bought the myrrh. Your Resources are not expended.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:00:37-08:00","id":1052909,"title":"","content":"OOC: Can I attempt two? If so, then yeah; if not, then I would rather focus on the tribesmen and the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488593\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488593\" target=\"_blank\"> Dice Roller &bull; Orokos.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488593\" target=\"_blank\"> http://orokos.com/roll/488593 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Orokos is a tool site for role-playing games, such as Dungeons and Dragons 4th edition, allowing players to upload characters from Wizards of the Coast's Character Builder program and providing a dice roller and attribute calculator. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But apparently I can't make heads or tails of it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488614\" target=\"_blank\">http://orokos.com/roll/488614</a> <div align=\"center\"><b>Antikatoprismos: </b><b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Obrimos Gnostikon of the Arcadian Mysteries</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast, Desert-Wise| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Health: OOOOOOO </b></span>| <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5 | <b>Mana:</b> 6/12</div> <br /> The ex-soldier scoffs. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Oh, who cares what those non-civilized bastards think. I defer judgment to someone who knows better. Just dress up as traveling scholars from the Academy, spread some wealth around, and call it a day.&quot; </span>He purses his lips. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Though I have to wonder if the Red Land is a metaphor of some kind... hmmm...&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","user":"Silver_Smoulder","date":". 02-21-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:10:52-08:00","id":1052916,"title":"","content":"[[you can attempt other rolls, yeah]]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:27:20-08:00","id":1053013,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Steadfast | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 7/15</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> After bidding his acquaintances a good day with a promise to return later, Khvarenah returned to the inn to begin his prayers and the kindling of the holy fire within. Again his tablet was at the center of it, yet this time it was the object itself that received the blessing. He began with a prayer to Vohu Manah, righteous purpose, for that is what he believed he had. He knelt before a fire and to it he commended a shard to pottery on which a word was graven. It had been a lot, which had once decided which of many soldiers would stand on the front lines and which would be placed farther back. The longer he chanted the more the tablet seemed to catch the light, until every edge was shining with a tiny cuneiform star.<br /> <br /> There was a little time after he finished his invocation of Voju Manah he overheard some of the rumors around town. This god, Sin, roused a memory. That was the name of Babylon's goddess of the moon. Might this have some relation?<br /> <br /> Later, when the hedge of the sky glistened with ten-thousand thousand silver thorns, he returned to the temple and found the priests where he expected them to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b><span style=\"color:#00008B\">How splendid are Mazda's lamps, or perhaps how beautiful is Nut who stretched herself across the sky. Many stories, but the stars do not seem to mind, appearing as one to all. There, Sopdet rises. It seems Isis smiles on this, the hour of our meeting.</span></b>&quot;<br /> <br /> He glanced at the sky, yet when he held up the tablet it seemed to be its own shard of the heavens, and many secrets writen faintly among the true stars were written clearly upon it in dancing rays.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Exceptional Luck to grant myself 8-again on Monkey's Paw, dismissed after Monkey's Paw<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency, +1 for 8-again, +2 to affect spellcasting<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0 (3 free), Duration -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Order Rote Skill + 6, Shadowname +2, Highspeech +2, Order Tool +1<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Rote Order Skill 6 + Shadow Name 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1 - Penalties 2 = 18.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488651\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> <br /> Casting Superlative Luck to add the rote quality to upcoming Monkey's Paw, Spending 1 Mana to mitigate nemesis, dismissed after Monkey's Paw<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency, +2 to apply to spellcasting<br /> Reach: 2 free, 1 over<br /> Factors: Potency - 0, Duration (primary) -0 (3 steps free), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Shadowname 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1, Dedicated Tool<br /> Nemesis: 3 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -3 from Mana/Tool. Contain. Nemesis roll <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488653\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Wisdom roll, not needed.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Shadowname 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1 - Penalties 0 = 14<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488654\" target=\"_blank\">6 success</a><br /> <br /> Casting Monkey's Paw to raise the dice bonus on the academic tool, 3 hours of casting, +10 bonus<br /> Ritual, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Advanced Potency, +1 for to break cap of 5<br /> Reach: 3 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -14 (3 free), Duration -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Order Rote Skill + 6, Shadowname +2, Highspeech +2, Order Tool +1<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Extra Time 5 + Rote Order Skill 6 + Shadow Name 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1 - Penalties 16 = 9.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488660\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes - Exceptional</a><br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ___________________________<br /> <br /> Casting Superlative Luck to add the rote quality to upcoming Astronomy roll<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Advanced Potency<br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency - 0, Duration (primary) -0 (3 steps free), Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Shadowname 2 + High Speech 2 + Path Tool 1, Sacrament +1 = 6<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Yantras 6 - Penalties 0 = 15<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488670\" target=\"_blank\">8 successes - Exceptional</a><br /> <br /> Casting Exceptional Luck to grant myself 8-again on upcoming Astronomy roll<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency, +1 for 8-again, +1 for 1 spell over gnosis<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0 (3 free), Duration -4, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Order Rote Skill + 6, Shadowname +2, Highspeech +2, Order Tool +1 = 11<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 +Arche 4 + Yantras 11 - Penalties 4 = 16.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488673\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes - Exceptional</a><br /> __________________________________________________ ___________________________<br /> <br /> Convince the priests I am not a threat but rather an exceptional scholar<br /> Manipulation 2 + Academics 5 + Tool 12 = 19<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488675\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a><br /> (Note: Forgot to apply -3 penalty. Three dice to the right are not successes)<br /> <br /> Astrology Roll, 8-again + rote quality<br /> Intelligence 3 + Academics 5 + Tool 12 = 20<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488677\" target=\"_blank\">18 succeses - Exceptional</a><br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ___________________________<br /> <br /> God called Sin<br /> Int 3 + Academics 5 + Tool 12 = 20<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488772\" target=\"_blank\">11 successes - Exceptional</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-22-2017, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T02:07:22-08:00","id":1053103,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: </b><b>L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 10/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Cratfing Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool),<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> Caught up in the Mystery he didn't even realize that Khvarenah had left, as he stands he looks at the priest standing near him. The pallor of his skin a little more ashen then before <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;No problem, this blood is old and dried, perhaps even predating this temple. Would I be allowed to visit the temple, I have been on the road for days and would relish a chance to pray in a holy place.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> If they let him in he will do his Oblation before the images of the Gods, if they do not then he will find the graveyard to to do his Oblations there. Either way after his <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488720\" target=\"_blank\">Oblations</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>3</b> he will return to the safe place.<br /> <br /> Back at the lodging he will present Kesmit with the \u200bMyrrh, and ask what the others have found, he will ponder the information and then attempt to tackle the <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488721\" target=\"_blank\">Streetwise</a>: <u>4d10h8</u> <b>0</b> (using up the Streadfast Condition here turning it to 1 success) and the <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488722\" target=\"_blank\">God Talk</a>: <u>4d10h8</u> <b>1</b> (1 success) from the list. Afterwords he will tell the rest that he needs to get some rest and lay down sore from his scouring.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Nile-based traders passing through the Red Land between cities in Egypt or Kush stick to routes defined by familiar landmarks and sometimes guard encampments, they don't really &quot;explore.&quot; Some are hoping that Hellenic rule will institute better patrols along the trade routes, like back when the old Dynasties had the strength to do that. It sounds like bandit activity has mostly been reduced since the Hellenes kicked the Persians out, which makes the recent robberies and killings by one particularly vicious band stand out more. [Int+Streetwise-1]</li> <li>Nomadic tribesmen interpret the Red Land as a collection of oases with relatively safe routes between each of them, like a storm with many eyes. They follow greater or lesser travel cycles between the oases, which is how they mark both distance and time. They talk about going &quot;shallow&quot; or &quot;deep&quot; into the Red Land, a measurement that is related to but distinct from how many oases you stop at (drink from?) during a journey. A long journey can be shallow, and a short journey can be deep. [Int+Occult-2 to interpret this.]</li> <li>Unlike the trading caravans, the tribesmen don't particularly venerate the gods of the Nile. They do show respect to Set and a lesser god called Ha, both of whom are represented at the Temple. A few of them quietly mention a divinity called Sin that lives deep in the Red Land, presumably a tribal patron god. [You can roll Int+Academics to make sense of all that god talk, or ask someone else.]</li> <li>Some of the traders swear they've seen one of the sha, the beasts of Set (in the way that a common jackal like Urbi is the beast of Anubis), padding alongside their caravan. The other traders are highly skeptical. [You can roll Int+Animal Ken+1, or Int+Occult-2, to interpet this.]</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-23-2017, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:10:50-08:00","id":1053696,"title":"","content":"The priests seem to have forgotten <b>Strife's </b>remarks about the blood almost as soon as they pass his lips. But allowing a fellow priest to rest and pray is completely reasonable, especially a friend of the enchanting Persian astrologer. The images of the gods in the innermost sanctum are off-limits, but they lead him into the temple proper where he can have some time alone to meditate on his Momentary Name and its ever-shifting relationship to Anpu, enigmatic Lord of the Afterlife.<br /> <br /> He's seated in front of a <a href=\"http://www.joanlansberry.com/setfind/sethibis.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">relief</a> of Set in battle with Apophis. The Hellenes think of Set as a malevolent god to be avoided, because they are a young empire, and they do not see the world as clearly as the Weret-Hekau. Set is Lord of the Red Land, of the desert, of storms, violence, disarray, and foreigners who bring all of them. But Set also guards the solar barge of Ra, spearing the true enemy of all-that-is: Apophis, the serpent of Chaos and bringer of what the Hellenes call Nemesis. It's a cosmic truth and a familiar scene, although for some reason, Set is depicted at Hibis with the head of a falcon (like Horus, his counterpart Lord of the Black Land) rather than the sha, his chosen beast.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Regain 3 Mana from Oblations. Also mark your Lethal damage on your Health header, replace the leftmost O with a bold <b>L </b>for resistant damage.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah </b>has a productive night of spellcraft and sorcery. With his righteous purpose assured by Vohu Manah, creative angel of guaranteed victory, he returns to the temple in the dark of night. Mitry and a cadre of other priests invite him inside the first and second archways into the inner courtyard. He has successfully persuaded the doubters that he is no spy or saboteur, but a devoted scholar, a passing star of fortune to be embraced rather than rejected. They will give him no further trouble.<br /> <br /> The mood is more serious tonight. The air is cool, the sacred pond as still as glass. They lead him up an undignified ladder to the flat top of one of the granary buildings: the highest point for many parasang, apart from the roof of the central temple hall itself. They provide him with a plumb line and notched palm branch to shut out starlight, even though his blessed tablet will do most of the work. They're expecting this to take hours, only the beginning of an extended star-charting process that could last all week. Plenty of time to get to know this enchanting stranger who has passed into their lives like an eclipse.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Roll results: your 4 exceptional successes on spellcasting were all prep for future rolls that you already factored, and you've already got the usual Fate bonuses, so I'll resolve the x-sux all at once and give you 5 Mana total. Magic makes the soul take flight.<br /> <br /> The hugely successful Astrology roll is a bit more special. Take the <b>Illuminated </b>Condition regarding the Mystery of the stellar convergence, which you can Scrutinize once it happens.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated</b><br /> You've been exposed to a Mystery, and now you're hungry for its secrets. Take +2 on any Scrutiny and Revelation rolls for the Mystery in question.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Fully reduce the Mystery's Opacity.<br /> <br /> Khvarenah regains 1 Mana for pursuing his Obsession, and the pot gets +1 Arcane Beat. It's now at 5.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The astrologer has his answer in minutes.<br /> <br /> The starlight and flickering torches illuminate his tablet in a certain way, showing him all the information he needs to match the night sky to the constellations in Ratri's dream-vision. This level of speed and precision for such a complex problem won't be available to Sleepers for millennia, but sometimes genius comes in a flash of inspiration. The convergence will take place on <b>Night 11 </b>of the rising of Aquarius.<br /> <br /> It should have been harder to determine. When he studies the night sky, Khvarenah is often frustrated by the dead places, the missing stars. The knowledge that <i>should </i>be readily available, but always proves elusive in ways a common astronomer couldn't explain. The promise of something vengeful hiding behind the last star chart. But tonight, somehow, the dark stars weren't in his way. Not one of them crossed the paths he needed to trace. It's theoretically possible, but the chances against it are staggering. He got very lucky.<br /> <br /> Very, very, very lucky. Like the whole game has been rigged.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Khvarenah's incredibly precise manipulation of Fate has not gone unnoticed. Take the <b>Star-Crossed </b>Persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Star-Crossed (persistent)</b><br /> Someone up there loves you. At the beginning of each chapter, the Storyteller rolls a dice pool equal to your Fate dots. Successes accumulate over the course of the story. Once the Storyteller has accrued a number of successes equal to your current Wisdom, something very exciting will happen.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Once per scene, take a Beat to invite the attention of a supernatural entity with an interest in Fate.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Let the Storyteller accrue successes, or uncover and counteract the Mystery on your own terms first.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As he sets his tools down in satisfaction, the gathered priests can't believe their eyes. They're not <i>impressed</i>, they're <i>shocked, </i>dumbstruck, baffled, afraid, angry. How the hell did he do that? Is this some kind of trick? Are the ancient and divine arts of astronomy being mocked by a foreigner? By a <i>sorcerer?</i><br /> <br /> He can feel his Fatebound strings unraveling. For all their wisdom, these priests are un-Wise, and they can't see the perfected works of the Amesha Spentas clearly. He's in a bit of a tight spot up here on the granary roof, surrounded by spooked and seething priests of a foreign religion. Mitry gestures for calm, but reaches out and demands that Khvarenah hand over the tablet so the priests can examine it at length and hold it for safekeeping.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Also, did I mention that using an item with an impossible equipment bonus (greater than +5) in front of Sleepers is cause for Dissonance? The priests have high Integrity and there's a few of them, so they rolled pretty hot. Monkey's Paw will end shortly as its Duration factor is reduced to one scene, and Serendipity also loses a Reach: now Mental can only substitute for Mental, Physical for Physical, or Social for Social.<br /> <br /> On that note, roll Manipulation+Persuasion-3 to fast talk and get out of the temple with your tablet. On a failure you'll have to either hand over the cuneiform tablet or lose your Allies dots, dramatic failure (which you can always choose for a Beat if you fail) means breaking the tablet in your escape.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Slightly more upbeat news for everyone else as they muse on the news Unbound brought back from the camp.<br /> <br /> <b>Prism </b>has nothing to add about the gods. But he has an insight about the Red Land. When the nomadic tribes talk about going &quot;shallow&quot; or &quot;deep&quot;, he thinks about the deep places of the world where spirits hold court. The spirit of the poplar grove still lives in the poplar grove, but a <i>deeper </i>part of it that passers-by don't see. Any traveler would have to drink from an oasis to survive a desert journey, but maybe drinking from the <i>right </i>ones is the key to going &quot;deeper&quot; into the Red Land. But what makes the right ones?<br /> <br /> <b>Strife </b>isn't sure he knows anything about bandits, but Fate pushes him to ask around the market when he picks up the myrrh, and things begin to solidify. The unusually vicious bandits are known to disguise themselves as ordinary traders to get close to other caravans in the wilderness. Beware of banners and saddlebags depicting a serpent encircling a jackal! The bandits are thought to have stolen their equipment from a trading family that uses that emblem.<br /> <br /> As for the gods: Set is much more prominent, as Strife was contemplating back at the temple, but Set and Ha are both gods of the desert. Ha is specifically the desert west of the Nile, which is where you are now. Whereas the desert east of the Nile is celebrated for fruitful seedings and life, the western desert is associated with tombs and the Underworld and the journey through the afterlife. Death is called &quot;going westward&quot; for a reason. Ha is a desert god, but also a Duat god.<br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah </b>is in fact quite familiar with Babylon, and the name Sin is known to him. He's god, not goddess, with a beard of lapis lazuli and a great winged bull for a mount. His worship is falling out of fashion in the time of Zarathustra, but he was once called the highest of the gods, the father of wisdom, teacher of astrology in the ever-changing faces of the moon.<br /> <br /> None of that explains why isolated tribesmen in the Egyptian desert would be paying homage to a fading Babylonian god. How would they even know about him? As Unbound related the story, it sounds like the tribesmen discuss Sin in more concrete terms than Set or Ha. The moon association is still there, but they describe Sin as feminine, and not at all a leader of other gods. No one claimed to have <i>seen </i>Sin, but it was discussed like a real possibility, and a terrible fate. They conceive of Sin as living &quot;deep&quot; in the Red Land specifically. She doesn't show her changing face much in the shallow parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:24:27-08:00","id":1053700,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Aquarius rising, Day 2</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">New day, new scene. You can spend today buying equipment at the market/camp/temple or making rolls or casting spells or whateva. First Condition you resolve this scene gives you a beat/arcane beat again.<br /> <br /> Things to think about<b></b>: Unbound will be making one roll per day to secure a desert guide, and will achieve that goal on Night 4 if left unattended. You can try to speed that process up by joining him at the camp, raising the Impression level through one of the various ways you do that, and making Social Maneuvering rolls yourself.<br /> <br /> Imhotep, what with that Contacts (Vampires), will probably be interested in the shadowy occult bloodstain Strife saw at the temple. He can roll Int+Occult to ponder what exactly this might mean.<br /> <br /> Remember: convergence is happening on Night 11, and the desert journey will take ??? days.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:29:04-08:00","id":1053944,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Inspired, Steadfast, Team Player | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 7/15</div><br /> <br /> Imhotep ponder the significance of the sha and the blood stain.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> In the camp, he tries to find rumours - what do nomads say about each other, and potential guides in particular? What makes them flow?<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> What is the significance of the sha? Int 3 + Occult 2 - obscurity 2 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489204\" target=\"_blank\">3d10h8, 0 succsesses</a>. I'll turn that into a dramatic failure for a beat.<br /> What about the blood stain? Int 3 + Occult 2 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489208\" target=\"_blank\">5d10h8, 3 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> Gathering rumors (eq building) Wits 2 + Socialize 2 - bonus 2 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489213\" target=\"_blank\">2d10h8, 0 successes</a>. I'd like Fragile, if you would.<br /> Figuring out Vice: Wits 2 + Empathy 1 + rumors 2 - difficulty 3 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489215\" target=\"_blank\">2d10h8, 0 successes</a>. Resolving Steadfast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:37:08-08:00","id":1054226,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed and Informed.<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 10/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath)<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> <br /> Upon waking he feels a little more refreshed, though his body still feels the pain from having pulled Hekau for his very pattern. His ashen pallor and slow movement shows this fact. After eating he will cast a few spells and decides to let Fate guide his action today. He will go to the market and pick up his Javelins from the Merchant and then go to the camp to assist in finding a desert guide.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Spell Casting<br /> Serendipity: He will allow Fate to guide him while helping Unbound find a Guide in the camps. So Serendipity will go to that task.<br /> <br /> <b>Improvised Imago:</b> Serendipity (Fate \u2022): Aid in the finding of a Desert Guide.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 2 (Arcane) +5 (Yantras) -2 (+1 Duration) -2 (+1 Potency) = 6 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 2, Reaches used: 2 (1 to change spell to Advanced Duration, 1 for Substitute Skills.)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Concentration, +2), (Mantras: High Speech, +2), (Dedicated Magic Tool: Ornate Mace, -2 Paradox, +1 Path Tool)<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489456\" target=\"_blank\">Serendipity</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>1</b><br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 0<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3 (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Day<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 1 Person<br /> <b>Range:</b> Self<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 1 hour.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Aid in the finding of a Desert Guide. <hr /><br /> Fools Rush In: Enter unprepared situations with grace an timing.<br /> <br /> <b>Improvised Imago:</b> Fools Rush In (Fate \u2022\u2022): Fate guides him in an unprepared situation.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 2 (Arcane) +5 (Yantras) -4 (+2 Potency) = 6 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 1, Reaches used: 2 (1 to change spell to Advanced Duration, 1 for Potency Bonus to Die rolls..)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Concentration, +2), (Mantras: High Speech, +2), (Dedicated Magic Tool: Ornate Mace, -2 Paradox, +1 Path Tool)<br /> <br /> <b>Nemesis:</b> 2 (1 over reaching), -2 (Dedicated Magic Tool). 1 Chance Die = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489461\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox Fools Rush In</a>: <u>1d10</u> <b>7</b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:Green\">Try to contain it if the roll is a success</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489460\" target=\"_blank\">Fools Rush in</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>1</b><br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 0<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 3<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Day (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 1 Person<br /> <b>Range:</b> Self<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 1 hour.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Fate guides him in an unprepared situation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-24-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:12:32-08:00","id":1054405,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 13/15</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Persian moved slowly, setting the tablet on the ground gently then straightened with raised arms to show he meant no harm.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">I did not accomplish this all at once just now. What you saw was the completion of much work that was already done. The trip he across the desert was long, and I spent those nights measuring the stars in preparation. The tablet records measurements which were made in Babylon, by myself and the royal astrologers, so that I need not make those measurements anew. The stars are very clear tonight and perhaps the influence of this holy place has aided me for what is often difficult came with much ease tonight.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Seeing he was not convincing he lowered his hands slightly and continued in a lower voice. &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">There is more, but you must swear to the god of this place and by the sun and by the lord of the afterlife to keep it secret. It is very dear to me and I would not have it spread around.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Once they had he pulled out the measuring rod he always carried. In this configuration, it resembled two lengths of wood bound together by a strip of sinew. Carefully he unwrapped them then turned the shorter length until it was perpendicular and bound both together again. He heard muttering but ignored it, Then he held it up for inspection.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">This is an item which my tribe devised but which I have improved. Notice there are measuring notches on both rods. By aligning one star with the lower arm of the crosspiece and another star with the upper arm, noting the marks on both as well as on the long arm, it is possible to take a measurement of angles between any two points whatever their orientation. I did not use it now because I did so in the desert where the other travelers would not understand it.</span>&quot; <div align=\"center\"><br /> ***</div> <br /> Back at the upper room he was troubled when he met his companions again.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">I have determined the time of the convergence. The stars will align as they were in the vision on the night that follows the ninth day hence.However, I must in good conscience tell you that my activities may have attracted the attention of something... unusual. I would appreciate if you would turn your arts toward examining me for signs of it or its nature.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He took a breath to steady himself.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">Now then, if you are again willing I will pray for our endeavors this day.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fast talk the priests<br /> Manipulation 2 + Persuasion 3 - penalty 3 =2<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489645\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a><br /> Resolving Steadfast to make it a success<br /> <br /> Didn't tell a single lie in that.<br /> <br /> Quick and Dirty Casting<br /> Exceptional Luck: 4 free reach, 1 for 8-again, 2 for affect spellcasting, 1 for instant cast<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489892\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes</a><br /> <br /> Casting Exceptional Luck rote to give us all the Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast conditions<br /> Instant, Sensory, Advanced Duration, Advanced Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -6, Duration -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Order Skill +6, High Speech +2, Shadowname +2, Order Tool +1 = 11<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 + Arche 4 + Yantras 11 - Penalties 8 = 12. Casting roll.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489893\" target=\"_blank\">6 Successes</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-25-2017, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T00:38:25-08:00","id":1054677,"title":"","content":"<b>Double Post</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:46:04-08:00","id":1055098,"title":"","content":"<b>Khvarenah </b>managed, by the skin of his teeth, to persuade Mitry and the other priests that he is no sorcerer. They were assuaged with a great deal of grumbling, but they did swear not to reveal his secret. He left the temple with his secret kept and his tablet intact.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <b><u>Day 2</u></b><br /> <br /> In the morning, <b>Prism </b>is leaving in a hurry. He cryptically mentions a new dream-vision, more personal than the one Ratri sent you here for, and says that he must leave at once for Meroe with the caravan that brought you here yesterday. He says that you or Ratri will hear from him again when he finds what he is looking for, but he cannot join you in the Red Land.<br /> <br /> <b>Imhotep</b> draws some conclusions about the rumors of the sha. It's well known that the true beasts of Set live far from human eyes, in the places where the living don't reach. Either the traders who claimed to have seen them along their usual routes are lying, or (more likely to your sorcerous insight) some wicked spirit is impersonating a divine animal. If you encounter any of these false sha yourself, you should kill them for sure. To let the mockeries live would be an insult to Set, and that's not a good way to start a long trip through his desert kingdom.<br /> <br /> Urbi: <span style=\"color:#FFD700\">&quot;Good call. I know Lord Anubis <i>hates </i>when spirits masquerade as divine emissaries.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Take the <b>Dead Certain </b>Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Certain</b><br /> You know an imposter when you see one. If you encounter one of the false sha, take -2 on any rolls to deal with them positively.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Kill one of the false sha.<br /> <br /> +1 Beat for dramatic failure, pot is now at 1.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After conferring with Strife about the nature of the bloodstain, he has an idea of what's going on. In his dealings with the undead, he's learned about a hidden brotherhood called the <b><i>khaibit</i></b>- literally &quot;the Shadows,&quot; named for that part of the soul that feeds on offerings for the dead. These creatures feed on blood, but they hold a sort of low honor. They are known to act as sellswords and mercenaries, protecting people who pay for their services. There could be a lot of business for a mercenary in a distant town full of superstitious merchants traveling through the desert. The bloodstain is probably meant to mark their territory, to warn rivals but also attract potential clients. If you went searching in the temple at night, you could probably arrange for one of these Shadows to protect your caravan from the unique dangers of the Red Land in ways that a mortal guide alone could not.<br /> <br /> Urbi: <span style=\"color:#FFD700\">&quot;I can Pathfind our way to this thing's parlor, but I don't know about this. There's always a price, and I don't think blood-drinkers need silver.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah </b>manages to bless the others for the day as he did yesterday, but his own Fate is more shadowy. He's welcome to scrutinize himself, especially if he can find a reflecting pool to watch himself in. Studying it from another perspective may have to wait until the others return, however. <b>Strife </b>does some Fate-alignment of his own, ritually preparing himself to be guided by his master Anpu. He looks out the window and focuses on a young boy dressed all in blue, and thinks: <i>I should ask someone like that about Clan Ibex.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Everyone renews Charmed, Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast. The first time you resolve one this scene/day, it grants an arcane beat.<br /> <br /> Strife can substitute Skills in the same category on 3 rolls today, and gets +3 dice on 3 rolls of his choice as long as they happen in the moment and aren't pre-planned. The group's Impression level with the camp improves from Good to Excellent, which allows one roll per hour instead of per day. They have 3 Doors currently.<br /> <br /> +1 Arcane Beat for Imhotep resolving Steadfast, pot is at 6.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Strife </b>and <b>Imhotep </b>go with <b>Unbound </b>to the camp. The mood isn't quite as jovial as it was last night. The camel that Unbound saw marked with a serpent coiled around a jackal and eating its own tail, the same sigil he saw on the murderous sorcerer who once tried to kill him, is gone today. The nomads at the camp whisper that it belonged to a pack of bandits called the <b>En-Sabah</b> who were mingling last night and spending blood money, but skipped town around sunrise.<br /> <br /> Following Strife's omen, they see an old man in a striking blue turban stirring a stew pot over a campfire, and ask him what he's heard about Clan Ibex. He waves them off at first, but a younger man passing by says they're all strange in the head, and too much time in the deep Red Land has cooked their brains. More people sit down and tell stories and rumors, and a free-flowing conversation starts up. This is not a stable situation, and Imhotep knows it: they can gather rumors here, but the men have no reason to stay, and the ongoing conversation will drift apart soon. Still, he does learn something useful.<br /> <br /> There's a man in Clan Ibex whom the gathered tribesmen call <b>Asyut</b>, and the ones who don't like his Clan grudgingly respect him. He's the only one with a good head on his shoulders, they say. Doesn't get swept up by superstition or worry too much about the gods or appeals to honor. Keeps his eyes on the horizon, very practical, some would say <b>Cynical. </b>If you wanted a skilled, experienced, and unafraid guide for the Red Land, you need to find someone who knows Asyut.<br /> <br /> A weathered and bearded man with his black hair (going gray) tied back with a ribbon is whittling something at the edge of the campfire. He's been ignoring the conversation so far, but he suggests that you should probably leave Asyut be. A man like him wouldn't have time for mysterious travelers with too much money who ask lots of questions, and besides, Clan Ibex is cooked in the head anyway. The other conversationalists agree, and start changing the subject. You know who's really crazy? Clan Hare. I heard that last winter, one of them picked a fight with a Greek soldier over a dice game...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T02:00:45-08:00","id":1055137,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (3/3):</b> Serendipity, Fools Rush In, Interconnections | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b> Exceptional Luck<br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath)<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> Strife will listen to the older man doing the whittling, doodling in the sand where he sits, he will then comment <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Then this Asyut is exactly the man we need and besides who said all we have to offer is money, for a guide like that we could provide other services in exchange. We are a group with many talents.&quot;</b></span></span> He will peer into the man's soul using the legacy attainment Soul Marks. Spending a point of Hekau he will look at the man's Momentary Name and surreptitiously scribbling it (making it look like part of his doodling) in the sand where he sits. He will contemplate the mans Momentary Name and beside it he will write the numerological equivalent derived from Gematria. Felling that the man may be connected to Asyut, could even be him. he will study the man.<br /> <br /> He begins looking at the strands of fate that interconnect all people, places and objects, studying each man that is involved in the conversation with them. Starting the the man whittling he will look for the strands that might lead to Asyut. He will also keep an eye out to see if anyone reacted to him casting a spell as they may be a mage as well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He is doodling during the conversation so that when he starts to draw the Momentary name and it's numerological equivalent it will just look like part of the doodling.<br /> I will make a roll to open the doors to find Asyut, spend 1 serendipity to shift the roll to Manipulation + streetwise and add +3 to the roll from Fools Rush In. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490245\" target=\"_blank\">Open Door</a>: <u>4d10h8</u> <b>0</b> resolving Steadfast Condition to turn that into a success and the Charmed Condition to turn it into an Exceptional Success opening 2 doors (if that is allowed, if not then just the Steadfast Condition).<br /> <br /> Use Dexterity + Stealth (switching weaponry to stealth) and using a second +3 <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490256\" target=\"_blank\">Surreptitiously Record Momentary Name</a>: <u>8d10h8</u> <b>2</b> Successes. Doing it subtly so as to not spook the others or the man, writing is sometimes considered unfavorably/suspiciously by the masses.<br /> <br /> The above is in preparation to subtly cast the Interconnection spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Rote Imago:</b> Interconnections (Fate \u2022): Look at interconnections of those involved in the conversation.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 2 (Arcane) +6 (Yantras) +3 (willpower) -4 (+2 potency) -2 (+1 scale) = 8 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 5, Reaches used: 4 (1 to move to instant casting, 1 to change spell to Advanced Duration, 1 for Advanced Scale, 1 spell specific reach to detect possession , mind control, altered destiny on targets)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Mudras, Investigation +3), (Sympathetic component Momentary Name +1), (numerological assessment +2)<br /> <br /> <b>Nemesis:</b> None (Unless being Surreptitious didn't work then 1 dice for witnessed by sleepers + 1 dice for second time this scene risking Nemesis = 2 dice (spending 2 Hekau to make it 1 chance dice) with rote quality) If I do risk Nemesis then try to contain it.<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand Trait</b>: Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490263\" target=\"_blank\">Interconnections</a>: <u>8d10h8</u> <b>4</b><br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4 (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 10 poeple<br /> <b>Range:</b> Self<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 3 turns.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Look at the interconnectivity of those involved in the conversation starting with the whittling man.<br /> <br /> I have used 2 of the Serendipity, 2 of the Fools Rush In bonuses and 1 mana</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-27-2017, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:47:54-08:00","id":1055329,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Inspired, Informed, Steadfast, Team Player, Dead Certain | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 7/15</div><br /> <i>OOC: this is assuming Strife finds Asyut</i><br /> <br /> Imhotep explains the situation, portraing Ratri and the cabal as mundane scolars (Khvarenah and himself) and their guards (Strife and Unbound), rather then sorcerers.<br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\">&quot;...and I must say, she would be terribly desolated if she were proven wrong.&quot;</span><br /> <hr /><br /> Goading Asyut to accept, spending WP: Man 3 + Empaty 1 + WP 3 + rumors 2 - attitude 3 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490369\" target=\"_blank\">6d10h8, 3 successes</a>. Resolving Inspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:40:00-08:00","id":1055705,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Okay, I'm back.<br /> I think there is 3 Doors total on the market, so after what Strife had done there's 1 or 2 still closed, depending on the Storyteller's decision. Anyway, I try to open the last one.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ever since they had entered the market, Unbound was observing the swarm of the people there, especially those that he rwas recognizing from last night - or those who eyed him with a knowing look. As one thing led to another, it was becoming more and more clear that Clan Ibex is not a comfortable subject for these folks and that if the right words aren't spoken, the whole town could turn on them. Accordingly, he tries to <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490639\" target=\"_blank\">soothe the nerves</a> of those attending.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;I understand your reluctance, we don't like craziness like this any more than you do, but by helping us you get rid both of us and - effectively - of Clan Ibex, for a snake cannot move without its head - and the head will be far into the desert. Again, you will be able to return to your lives with no one botherting you&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I do the above to open (one of) the last Door(s), of course.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 02-27-2017, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:18:30-08:00","id":1056461,"title":"","content":"The crowd finds it strange when <b>Strife </b>starts sketching in the sand. Not everyone notices in the bustle, but there's no good reason for a decent person to be drawing strange symbols unless they're some kind of travel map. And only a sorcerer would write someone's <i>ren</i> without their permission.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The crowd passed a perception check so you did risk Nemesis, but got no successes on the chance die. You spent 2 Hekau but no other bad stuff happened.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer you only resolve one success-upgrading Condition per roll, so you resolve Steadfast but keep Charmed.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It doesn't seem to have drawn the eyes of Apophis, though. Empowered by <i>ren, </i>the warrior'smagic arises in the world and illuminates the lifeweb of the crowd to his sight. Almost everyone gathered right now has Medium sympathy to each other, bound by a network of clan ties and family relationships. Imhotep's jackal, Urbi, is ridden by a divine spirit that knows its borrowed body very well. Your companion called Unbound is, of course, possessed by the awoken demon of his own Cruelty, but that's by his own hand. An older woman in a colorful headwrap, standing quietly among a chatty group and nervously fingering an amulet in her pocket, seems to have been hexed. Her Fate is cloudy like unclean water. But at least she's part of a network of shared Sympathy.<br /> <br /> The whittling man stands out, because he has only thin ties to the rest of this group of people. He's more than a stranger, but not a friend. They don't know him well. While the others gossip about Clan Ibex as outsiders, he works and watches the horizon and listens. He has no special destiny or curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbound </b>makes his case for letting the strangers and the Ibex take care of each other, and the crowd likes it. They nod and people start to disperse, saying that they'll find Asyut and bring him to you and all this will be done with. As the crowd breaks up to go looking, the whittling man puts away his carving, gets up, and- almost as an afterthought- jerks his head at the three sorcerers. He wants you to follow.<br /> <br /> He leads you a little past the edge of camp, to a palm tree on the edge of the oasis where he has a camel tied. He thinks for a minute, then speaks up: <span style=\"color:#008000\">&quot;I am Asyut. Make your case.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>Imhotep </b>makes the case. Urbi helps. The emissary of Anpu curls up and lets him scratch behind her ears, which turns out to be just the thing to make him open up. It seems like Asyut has a <b>Protective </b>impulse.<br /> <br /> In the end, he's persuaded after you lay out the broad strokes of what you're trying to do. To be clear, he thinks this is a fool's errand, but you seem sincere. He'll do it for a hefty quantity of silver, up front, and a sworn assurance that you will somehow put him in contact with Ratri when you return. He wants to hear for himself what some foreign scholar wants in the Red Land.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Because of your exceptional success, Asyut is willing to act as guide for a Resources 3 purchase.<br /> <br /> +1 Arcane Beat for Imhotep resolving Inspired, pot is at 7.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:40:34-08:00","id":1058087,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 13/15</div><div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b>Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</div><br /> After his confrontation with the priests and the sense of being perceived that had come over him. Once the others had left he took out the shallow bowl of polished copper he used for prayer. He filled it with pure water that Kesmit had thoughtfully drawn and sat down. He closed his eyes and the world grew dark and then he <i>opened</i> them and in the shadowed room there was light. The shadows grew darker, the tiny spots of light brighter, and for a moment he hallucinated that he hung in the midst of a lake of stars.<br /> <br /> His prayers were in a mix of his native tongue and the masterful speech he had learned from the true sorcerers of the karpani, blending them together into something like music, both a declaration and a request. What had seen him he could see. What had marked him he could mark. And, perhaps, this would give him one more clue to the reason his master had sent him. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 mana to activate Active Mage Sight and viewing the reflection of my nimbus in the bowl as I cast the following spells:<br /> <br /> <br /> Casting Interconnection to examine myself<br /> Instant, Sensory, Standard Duration, Standard Scale, Advanced Potency<br /> Reach: 4 free, 0 over, 2 for specific details<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0 (3 free steps), Duration -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Shadowname +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrement +1 = 6<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 + Arche 4 + Yantras 6 - Penalties 0 = 15. Casting roll.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492263\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/489893\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>Casting Correspondance to examine myself, looking for the thing that is watching me, spending one mana for improvised spell from a non-ruling arcana<br /> Instant, Sensory, Standard Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 3 free, 0 over, 2 to find something specific<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0 (2 free steps), Duration -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Shadowname +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrement +1 = 6<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 + Arche 3 + Yantras 6 - Penalties 0 = 14. Casting roll.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492263\" target=\"_blank\">8</a><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492265\" target=\"_blank\"> Successes</a> - Exceptional </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:13:53-08:00","id":1058204,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath)<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div><hr /><br /> <br /> After finding the guide Strife heads back to the sanctum, where he sees Khvarenah meditating and casting spells. Not wanting to interrupt he slips back out and heads to the market. Looking for Unbound and Imhotep to help with the shopping. The three can head to the market. Asking around he inquires where to purchase the best in Desert gear. He will need to purchase enough gear to outfit and service 5 people, this will be a minimum of two tents Nomad garb etc. The price is steep but it is needed to keep everyone safe and healthy in the deep desert.<br /> <br /> Before heading over to the Temple he will ask Unbound if he could magically enhance his intelligence and medical abilities so that he can acquire the medical supplies needed for the trip.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I didn't want to go to far as I am depending on others to join and help me. I don't like to assume that they will go.<br /> <br /> I didn't list all of the gear needed as I do not personally know what is needed.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:13:32-08:00","id":1058820,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Unbound heads to the market with Strife, allowing him to haggle for the desert equipment. He has restricted himself to looking out for the crowd, paying attention to undesired elements, especially thieves and sleazy beggars. He is not getting robbed, not in this dump.<br /> <br /> (OOC: I can't find the information if Unbound is aware of the temple bloodstain and what it implies. If yes, while at the market he asks Strife (and Imhotep, if he's there) if we should seek assistance from these &quot;Shadows&quot;. If he doesn't know anything, he simply asks about their time in the temple)<br /> <br /> When Strife makes his request, Unbound complies with it. He asks for the two of them to find a quiet spot, slightly touches his cloak, spills some clean water on the ground and intones the incantations in High Speech. The business is concluded when he touches Strife's forehead with two fingers, feeling potent magic flow through him, cold and bracing like a mountain stream.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Casting Augment Mind to improve Strife's Intelligence<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration (a day), Standard Scale, Standard Potency (2)<br /> Reach: 1 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0, Duration -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 - Penalties 4 = 6 Casting roll.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492640\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492640\" target=\"_blank\"> Dice Roller &bull; Orokos.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492640\" target=\"_blank\"> http://orokos.com/roll/492640 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Orokos is a tool site for role-playing games, such as Dungeons and Dragons 4th edition, allowing players to upload characters from Wizards of the Coast's Character Builder program and providing a dice roller and attribute calculator. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Casting Enhance Skill to improve Strife's Medicine<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration (a day), Standard Scale, Standard Potency (2)<br /> Reach: 1 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Duration (primary) -0, Potency -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 - Penalties 4 = 6 Casting roll.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492641\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492641\" target=\"_blank\"> Dice Roller &bull; Orokos.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492641\" target=\"_blank\"> http://orokos.com/roll/492641 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Orokos is a tool site for role-playing games, such as Dungeons and Dragons 4th edition, allowing players to upload characters from Wizards of the Coast's Character Builder program and providing a dice roller and attribute calculator. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 03-06-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:55:48-08:00","id":1058829,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath)<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div><hr /><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes Strife told everyone of the Blood stain, as far as I know strife doesn't know anything of vampires or that what he saw in his revaluation was the work of a vampire.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I am assuming that the Attribute needed to go with medicine is intelligence, let me know and I will make the roll and add it to this post.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Strife thanks unbound for the spells and when asked about the shadows and if they should be asked for assistance his only look is of worry, there is no telling what these shadows will do once we are alone with them in the desert. He suggests caution when dealing with the shadows and not to do it alone. He leaves Unbound and proceeds to the temple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:03:01-08:00","id":1059345,"title":"","content":"<b>Khvarenah </b>is sitting in the lake of stars. With his Fate Sight alone, he recognizes something different. Rather than the presence of a great Destiny and Doom, or even the simple clarity of a man with no special Destiny, he has something hollow.<br /> <br /> The Fate of any particular person or kingdom or holy relic is described in their particular stars, their horoscope. The stars move as an ordered system in the patterns laid out for them, perhaps by the Moirai, certainly by some wise divine actor. When he Awakened, he saw their silver rays of starlight as Thorns in a hedge, and as he developed his Gnosis he realized that these silver Thorns are the expanding possibilities and timelines that each star ordains for the world. But as the magician has learned, there are dark stars that move like planets (literally &quot;wanderers&quot; in Greek) in ways that cannot be accounted for. Sometimes these dark and restless stars cross the proper orbits of the bright stars, moving retrograde (going westward, which of course symbolizes death to the Weret-Hekau) and leading otherwise fruitful Destinies to rot unfulfilled and unworthy men to rise in station. This is how an astronomer understands Fate- hedge witches and soothsayers might interpret things differently, but they do not see the world as clearly as he does.<br /> <br /> With his Unveiling Fate spell, Khvarenah sees that one of these absent stars has somehow fixed itself in his horoscope. In the place where he would expect to see a Thorn to read his Destiny and Doom from a prominent star, he sees a small rent in the tapestry. This anti-Destiny consumes and destroys purpose, and as he entangles his fate more closely with others, the tear will unbalance and destroy those fates as well. The hollow tear defies his efforts to scrutinize it with Fate, because it is no Fate at all. But he knows enough to guess that the more he manipulates his own personal Fate through sorcery, the tear will grow wider and affect those fates which do not touch his as closely. For now, he is the only one in danger.<br /> <br /> He has better insight with Knowing Space, approaching the problem with a different set of tools. He does have a sympathetic link that emerged from this watching presence. It's barely visible, drowned out by the starlight. But when he adjusts his perception just right, the darkness of the absent star reveals something hidden. He sees a thread extending from his chest out into the reflecting bowl (and back to him from the bowl in his reflection). Khvarenah has a Weak sympathetic link to the thing that is observing him, and it is not within sensory range. He pushes his magic to its limit, and a Space-granted vision emerges in the reflecting bowl. He sees, very clearly, a Hellenic-style ceramic statue of a great fish pouring water from its open mouth. It obviously represents the sign of <b>Pisces. </b>The current astrological month is Aquarius, Pisces will be rising next month.<br /> <br /> Khvarenah has a sinking feeling that someone is screwing with him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Khvarenah has a Weak sympathetic tie to...a statue of Pisces somewhere in Hellas! Or someone is deceiving him! Maybe! You don't currently have a sympathetic yantra for spellcasting along this link, but you can always examine the link itself and do other fun stuff with it. +1 Arcane Beat for stumbling on something interesting and magical that you can pursue further, pot is at 9 now.<br /> <br /> Here's some game mechanics stuff relating to the tear: it's a Mystery, Opacity 4, which cannot be scrutinized with Fate Sight, although another Arche may work. Any mage who sees Khvarenah's Nimbus can attempt to scrutinize or reveal it. Following some rules from the Signs of Sorcery preview, the tear is Locked. You or another PC will have to learn some Surface Information using Focused Sight before you can reduce the Opacity.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, thanks to <b>Unbound</b>'s magic, <b>Strife</b> sees more clearly. His Mind is clear and sharp, and he feels as confident as a master healer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unless something is specifically a secret, I find games work better when the PCs can discuss what they know in-character. I assume Imhotep has broadly told the others about the Shadows, leaving out the details of his personal experiences. You guys probably don't think of &quot;vampires&quot; as a distinct category of creature with their own culture and society, even if you've encountered monsters that drink blood.<br /> <br /> Strife has Intelligence 5 and Medicine 5 for the rest of the day. Getting the supplies will be Intelligence+Medicine with a -2 for Availability 2, and also a -3 for coldness as the priests are less excited about working with you guys after last night.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He arrives at the temple in the late afternoon. The priest Mitry whom you've already met is in the outer courtyard and willing to chat for a few minutes. They do keep bandages and tools and salves and other medical supplies here, but he wants to know what exactly you need them for. If someone is sick or injured, why not bring them to the temple yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-07-2017, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:49:01-08:00","id":1059721,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath)<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> As he receives the cold reception he will ask <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Why the coldness towards a fellow priest and countryman&quot;</b></span>. If they mention the weirdness with Khvarenah he will explain </span><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;He is just a travelling companion sharing the road with me and my wife, We travel into the Red Land as my wife and I have both received visions from our Lord Anpu to seek mysteries in that land. There is strength in numbers when traveling in such hostile lands. I have come to ask for bandages and salves as my wife is more fair skinned than I and I need to protect her. I would travel without her but the Vision that we received showed the two of us standing before a great stone hand in the desert, I feel Anpu wishes us both to go. I would be glad to share any mysteries that I uncover from this strange vision and the travels into the Red Lands.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\">Hoping that they are a little more at ease with him, it would be a shame if he was at odds with his own people and priests to boot. </span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/493386\" target=\"_blank\">Int+Med roll</a>: <u>5d10h8</u> <b>1</b> received one success but will use Charmed Condition to turn the one success into an Exceptional success, The medical supply are important.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:07:26-08:00","id":1060214,"title":"","content":"Luck is on <b>Strife</b>'s side, and the priests are sympathetic. They've been wary because of all the excitement and strangeness from your party in the last day, but a fellow priest following a vision from a god they know is something they can get behind. They're willing to share their tools in a canvas bag.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You get the medical supplies, and the group can make Medicine rolls out in the field. Imhotep will be happy.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They're especially interested in hearing about any visions or revelations you see out in the Red Land. None of these educated men have ever heard of the great stone hand you describe, and they sadly can't offer any help there. However, Mitry brings up the rumors you've heard about the sha, the elusive beasts of Set, stalking the trade lanes. He suggests a reward, &quot;knowledge stored here that a priest of Anpu would value,&quot; if you can bring one of these sacred animals back to the Temple alive at the end of your journey. If you swear to capture (&quot;protect&quot;) one of the sha, the priests will offer a special prayer to Set and Ha, lords of the Red Land, for protection on your journey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T01:23:51-08:00","id":1060453,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div><hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;I thank you for your assistance and my the Blessing of Anpu be upon you and yours. If I see a sha I will try to capture it alive and bring it back. Nothing short of it threatening my wife will get me to harm it. That is the best that I can promise.&quot;</b></span> Thanking the priests for their assistance he will head back to the temporary residence.<br /> <br /> When he returns and sees that </span><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\">Khvarenah is still at work studying something about himself he will activate his death sight to see if he can get a glimpse. Seeing some weird patterns all jumbled up in his nimbus he becomes fascinated. Now he focuses his sight to see if he can read the surface of the patterns but sadly he can not. </span><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;There is something <span style=\"font-size:12px\">truly</span> amazing going on in your nimbus but sadly I can not see what.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/493934\" target=\"_blank\">Fate Mystery</a>: <u>2d10h8</u> <b>0</b> - Failure</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T11:38:28-08:00","id":1060581,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 7/15</div><br /> Imhotep will ask Unbound to boost his Manipulation and Ride, and then go to the camp.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:11:56-08:00","id":1060625,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <br /> Focusing his Mage Sight on Khvarenah's aura, Unbound instantly knows that something is amiss, out of place and yet, each time he almost had it, it slipped though his fingers. If only he could pull some mental thread to unravel this whole mess...<br /> <br /> Anyway, after Imhoteps enters their abode and asks for magical assistance, he complies without much hesitation. The tiniest bit of smoke leaves his fingers and quickly dissipates as the spell takes effect - the doctor will be now a lot more convincing and skilled at riding animals, at least for a time. If there are no further requests or other things that require his attention, Unbound lies on his bed with the intention of getting a good night's sleep. It's going to be a big day tomorrow, he was sure.<br /> <br /> (OOC: If nothing prevents it, Unbound will cast the Incognito Presence at sunrise and go straight to the temple. He will look for bloodstains on the floor, but also for anything resembling an archive, in which some information on these &quot;Shadows&quot; may be stored and for an entrance to the underground section, if any.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494112\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Augment Mind to improve Imhotep's Manipulation<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration (a day), Standard Scale, Standard Potency (2)<br /> Reach: 1 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0, Duration -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 - Penalties 4 = 6 Casting roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494110\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Enhance Skill to improve Imhotep's Ride<br /> Instant, Touch, Advanced Duration (a day), Standard Scale, Standard Potency (2)<br /> Reach: 1 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Duration (primary) -0, Potency -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 - Penalties 4 = 6 Casting roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494149\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Incognito Presence <br /> Ritual, Self, Advanced Duration (1 day), Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over (use 1 Reach to activate additional effect)<br /> Factors: Potency -0, Duration (primary) -2, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech, Order Tool, Sacrament<br /> Nemesis: None<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + High Speech 2 + Order Tool 1 + Sacrament 1 - Penalties 2 = 8<br /> (the effect of an exceptional success would be that I gain the Inspired Condition again, if you allow)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Focused Mage Sight using Mind <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494125\" target=\"_blank\">fails</a>. If you allow, I'd use Inspired to turn it into a simple success.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T17:20:25-08:00","id":1061386,"title":"","content":"<b>Unbound</b> quickens <b>Imhotep'</b>s faculties, and sends him off on his errand. While studying <b>Khvarenah</b>'s peculiar Nimbus through his Mind Arche, he gets no further than <b>Strife</b> did at first. But in a moment of inspiration, he has a sudden insight into the inter-related nature of the Archae. This Mystery can be approached through the eyes of Death.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Auto-success is Steadfast not Inspired, but yes that's fine. 10 Arcane Beats currently.<br /> <br /> Fast-forwarding through the next bit to move us along.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> After a productive day going between Camp and Market and Inn and exchanging money and honeyed words along the way, the group has secured Asyut's services (in exchange for a promise that you will introduce him to Ratri when this is over) as well as some more impressive camels and various survival equipment. You have the advanced survival gear, the better-trained camels, the torches, the medical equipment, and Asyut's services as a guide as described earlier.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Day 3 - Dawn </b><br /> <br /> It's a busy time to be at the Temple. Even this far from the Nile, the priests at Hibis do the most important ritual work of the day when the rising chariot of Ra passes through the sacred gates and archways into the holy place. The temple complex is bustling with priests, chanting, preparing anointing oils. But with their eyes focused on the divine, they simply don't notice a pack of hidden sorcerers. They are looking up, and Unbound has brought you below.<br /> <br /> With Urbi's keen nose to guide the group, they slip inside the main temple building interior just as the sun is rising. The archive of scrolls is in here, in a room along the southern wall beneath an image of Thoth, and it won't be in use for an hour or so while the priests are busy. It's dim and shadowy in here, among the unfamiliar maze of tall wooden racks and low stone desks. The light of the still-rising sun hasn't fully reached this side room yet. Still, there's enough to read with some difficulty. Urbi paws at the tiled stone floor and sniffs. Maybe there's a hidden chamber or trap door in here somewhere.<br /> <br /> You are in a dark maze-archive in a sacred temple, looking for clues about shadowy blood-drinking mercenaries. What do you do?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Anyone who wants to be in the Temple library is there, under the effect of Unbound's Incognito Presence. Here's some things you could do:<ul><li>Wits+Crafts to search for a hidden door.</li> <li>Wits+Academics-3 to find any information about the Shadows among the scrolls, 10 minutes per roll</li> <li>Matter or other magic to find hidden passages</li> <li>Mage Sight to scope out the room.</li> </ul><br /> The area is under the Poor Light tilt, giving -2 to any rolls requiring sight. This applies to the Crafts and Academics rolls I mentioned. You have, at most, 1 hour before the priests return to the library and notice some kind of disturbance, Incognito Presence or not.<br /> <br /> For scale purposes, the library counts as a large room. Urbi has spent 1 Essence to use Pathfinder.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:50:38-07:00","id":1061497,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div><hr /><br /> With the dark conditions he feels that fate can guide him to finding whatever he needs so he casts Quantum Flux to negate the near dark conditions. Searching the room he finds nothing in here.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Rote/Praxis/Improvised Imago:</b> Quantum Flux (Fate \u2022): Allow Fate to guide his hand to where he needs to be<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 2 (Arcane) +3 (Yantras) -2 (+1 potency) = 6 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 2, Reaches used: X (1 to move to instant casting, 1 to change spell to Advanced Duration)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Mantras: High Speech, +2), (Dedicated Magic Tool: Ornate Mace, -2 Paradox, +1 Path Tool).<br /> <br /> <b>Nemesis:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand Trait</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495226\" target=\"_blank\">Quantum Flux</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>3</b> = Success. He can negate a penalty of -2 for 2 rolls.<br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 0<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 2<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Day (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 1 Person<br /> <b>Range:</b> Self<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 2 turns.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Negate penalties.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495227\" target=\"_blank\">Look for hidden doors</a>: <u>5d10h8</u> <b>0</b> = Failure to find the hidden door.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T15:29:45-07:00","id":1061627,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><br /> Unbound ruffles through the scrolls for a minute, but quickly realizes that it's hopeless. There's too many of them, he doesn't know what he is looking for exactly and searching libraries was never his strong suit to begin with. If Strife or Imhotep won't find anything, probably no one will. However, as he touches the cold stone walls of the temple looking for a hidden passage and is about to give up, something guides his hand just where it needs to be, and judging by the sound of the screeching mechanism there is now a new path open nearby, leading - he can only presume - to the Shadows' lair. Beckoning those with him and jumping headfirst into the ominous darkness he only hopes that whatever lies on the other side of this tunnel will truly be weaker during daylight hours.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Resolving Charmed to find the passage (I assume there is one to begin with and that an average adult human can pass through it without a problem)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 03-12-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T18:17:27-07:00","id":1061667,"title":"","content":"Luck isn't on Strife's side. Even with Fate guiding his hands to the most likely places, he finds nothing hidden. The chanting and singing continues outside.<br /> <br /> How many shadows should be moving on the floor? There's five of you, right?<br /> <br /> Unbound, hopelessly tracing the stone, nearly trips as his foot catches something cut into the floor. Everyone feels something like a chime in their Periphery- magic was at play just now.<br /> <br /> One of the stone slabs fits loosely into the floor, and it slides easily along a carved track once you know where to look. A stroke of luck from Khvarenah's magic. Unbound, and anyone who follows him, climbs down into the passageway. The priests will certainly notice the open trapdoor if one of them enters the archive. Does someone stay outside to stand guard? Urbi could, although she doesn't have thumbs to reopen the trapdoor if you close it. She cautions you: &quot;Be very careful. You're entering a dangerous situation, even with magic to hide you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The passageway is mud brick walls and a packed earth floor, not the fine stone of the temple. Maybe it wasn't included in the floorplan. It's cold as soon as you drop down into it, and cramped- you almost need to crouch. The only light is a hazy square from the open tile. From where you stand, it looks like the passage goes westward about 15 yards before opening up into a larger space.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yep and yep. +1 AB for Charmed, 11 in the pot.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10396_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10396\" data-vbnamecard=\"10396\">Woland</a> roll a Clash of Wills with Mind, +1 for your spell's Duration. Something is pressing up against your Incognito Presence on the group.<br /> <br /> Everyone, be sure to state whether you're in the passageway or outside. There's still a -2 Poor Light penalty in the archive, which increases to -3 in the passageway.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:32:09-07:00","id":1061832,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (0/3):</b> | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> As they are discussing who will stay in the room Strife will cast a spell that will wedge the door shut. When moving back to the group he will count the shadows out of habit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>If he sees and extra shadow he will address it</b></span><br /> <br /> Raising his hands in a none threatening manner <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;Looks like we will not need to go into the tunnel after all, as the one we are searching for is here. Show yourself as we will not harm you as long as you mean us no harm. Can someone deaden the sound so that we may talk without <span style=\"font-size:12px\">alerting</span> the <span style=\"font-size:12px\">priests</span>.&quot;</b></span> he will wait for them to reveal himself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>OR if there is no extra shadow he will continue.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;</b></span></span><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Urbi you go with them I can stay up here as cloak the entrance or bar them from entering this room for a while. I can solidify the shadows in this area around the door and cause it to jam the door shut. or simply deepen the shadows in this room to conceal the trap door. But you all need to go so that I can cast the spell.&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> As the others disappear beneath he will continue to look around the room.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rolling perception to see count the shadows on the floor I will use the Last application of Quantum Flux to negate the low light condition penalties.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495665\" target=\"_blank\">Perception</a>: <u>5d10h8</u> <b>3</b> = Success<br /> <br /> <b>Rote Imago:</b> Shadow Crafting (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 3 (Arcane) +1 (Yantras) = 7 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 3, Reaches used: 3 (1 to move to instant casting, 1 to change spell to Advanced Duration, 1 to change spell to Advanced Scale.)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Dedicated Magic Tool: Ornate Mace, -2 Paradox, +1 Path Tool).<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495674\" target=\"_blank\">Shadow Craft</a>: <u>7d10h8</u> <b>3</b> = Success<br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> X (X Reduce Nemesis dice, 1 Spell Requirements, 1 Improvised Spell)<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> X<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 week (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 1 large wedge<br /> <b>Range:</b> Touch<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 1 turn.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> use the shadows near the door to form a wedge and wedge the door shut from the inside. Since the shadow form to the object before solidifying the bottom of the wedge is form fitting to the floor and should match the texture creating a especially stationary wedge.The wedge has a durability of 2.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:15:07-07:00","id":1062012,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Unbound feels the pressure on his spell, a gut-wrenching sensation of being looked at by someone... or something. Focusing every effort on upholding the magic, he hopes that it will be enough, and they will be able to continue unnoticed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495851\" target=\"_blank\">Clash of Wills</a>. Spending a point of Willpower to boost the pool by +3. Unless it's evident that there is something in the shadows and that something sees them, Unbound will hush Strife,not wanting to take any chances.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> IF there is a person looking at them and the Incognito Presence fails,he, too, adresses the being with a harsh tone: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;Come out, Shadow. We have business to discuss.&quot; </b></span>As he does this, helays his right hand on the hilt of his sword,slowly and steadily to not attract attention. Ifpossible without alerting the Shadow, he will also try to close in on it,one step at a time.<br /> <br /> IF however there is no Shadow or it looks past them, Unbound nods to Strife and descends underground, as first in the line. Just to be sure, with a small gesture he conjures some simple magic on everyone in the group (including Strife), but the effect is staggering - he immediately sees,hears and smells everything around him, like painted on a canvas, and presumes everyone else does too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495872\" target=\"_blank\">Casting </a>The Outward and Inward Eye<br /> Ritual, Touch, Advanced Duration (an hour), Advanced Scale (5 subjects), Standard Potency <br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Duration (primary) -0, Potency -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 2 + Yantras 4 = 9 Casting roll.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:54:34-07:00","id":1062710,"title":"","content":"It was just a trick of the light in the archive. When <b>Strife</b> looks more closely, he realizes there's no one up here but the sorcerers and Urbi, who is sitting on the floor listening carefully to the action below. It's probably wise to stand guard. With the door stuck shut with solid shadow, you'll have warning at least.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbound,</b> and anyone else down in the tunnel, isn't so lucky. The Shadows have supernaturally keen senses in their own lair, even when Ra is ascendant and night is ending.<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone </b>feels the cold chill of magic in their Periphery. Hands rest on hilts. A few paces down the tunnel from Unbound, the darkness ripples like the wake of a ship- and now there is a young man, half-starved, standing on the <i>ceiling </i>and looking up at you from his head hanging down at the floor. His eyes shine like a cat's.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;No further.&quot;</span> He sounds no older than a boy, but as confident as a man. Thin and bony and <i>so </i>hungry. The darkness that cloaks him flows when he speaks. This dark tunnel feels like standing in a shallow stream.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;The master sleeps. Why are you here?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> (The voice of Cruelty lurks in Unbound's ear: <i><span style=\"color:#8B4513\">&quot;weak. kill this one.&quot;</span></i><span style=\"color:#8B4513\">)</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unbound's demon offers him a chance to satisfy his Vice, as per his first Attainment. +1 bonus Willpower above your normal limit (and Guilty) if you accept, take Inspired (Negotiating) if you resist.<br /> <br /> Any spells to affect the lowercase-s shadows down in the tunnel with magic require a Clash using Gnosis+Death.<br /> <br /> Remember you can always use Mage Sight!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T09:27:20-07:00","id":1062823,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain | <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 6/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 6/15</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Imhotep opens his sight to the magical energies of this place and its inhabitants, pauses, then turns his attention to mundane sences.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\">&quot;We are travellers to the Red Land, oh Shadow, coming to ask your master if he's willing to help guard our caravan - or to lend your help in guarding it, as the matter stands. If any of you demand a payment, I'm ready to part with as much of my blood as you will need.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He feels his limbs stiffen as he wills hekau out of his flesh.<br /> <hr /><br /> Activating Mage Sight (Death, Life), taking a look to ascertain the youth'es (?) nature, then deactivating again.<br /> <br /> Making a polite impression: Pre 2 + Socialize 2 (or is it Persuasion? no difference anyway) + WP 3 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496529\" target=\"_blank\">7d10h8 <b>1</b></a> resolving Informed<br /> <br /> Scouring Pattern for -1 Dex, gaining 3 Hekau.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:43:49-07:00","id":1062981,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\">For a second, Unbound was actually inclined to put this creature out of its misery and grasped the hilt of his weapon a little tighter. Imhotep's voice, however, pulled him out of Cruelty's influence.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;To hell with you. I don't take orders from you&quot;</span></i> Only after he finished the sentence did he realize that his lips were moving. Nobody have seen it, though - the pitch-black darkness had its uses, after all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;This is no Shadow, merely a grain of sand on its sandals. We can negotiate a price, but only after you prove you are actually worth all those stories. So lead us to this 'master' of yours, lest you will be gutted like a pig!&quot;</b></span> Unbound was enraged at this man's impertinence, but also more than a little unnerved by the fact that he was able to sneak up on them like that.</div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:07:37-07:00","id":1063357,"title":"","content":"<b>Imhotep </b>sees truly. His enhanced senses alone can't overcome how dark this place is, but he picks some details out in the light of the trapdoor.<br /> <br /> With Life, he sees that the only living things in this place are the sorcerers. Points of warm, pulsing light in the darkness.<br /> <br /> With Death, he recognizes the curse of those who walk after death, sometimes called &quot;the ones who can't stop.&quot; This wretched creature has no soul, but the shattered remains of his <i>sheut </i>have clotted and spread to take its place. The shadows that surround this thing are moving like flowing blood. There is an animating intelligence behind the darkness circling their feet. The shadows are <i>part </i>of him. His corpse cannot contain his <i>sheut.</i><br /> <br /> There's a separate phenomenon here. He can't see it clearly, but all along the walls and deeper down the tunnel, he feels something heavy pulling down into the earth. It's akin to the Anchors that keep a ghost from passing on, but different in kind. As a Moros, he sees Death and Matter at once, and he sees that the heaviest points are marked by carved notches.<br /> <br /> The Shadow listens to Imhotep's appeal, possibly with interest, but his face doesn't react like a human's would. But apparently there's enough humanity there to rise to <b>Unbound</b>'s taunt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;No, Greek.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>Everyone </b>feels magic in their Periphery. Down in the tunnel, the Shadow bends backward and clutches the ceiling like a spider as the shaft of light grows as thin and faint as a pinhole. You can see nothing, but you feel the darkness itself become cold and heavy, like thick fog. Its voice is not coming from anywhere in particular.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;The master lies in <i>henet</i>, as he has since your soldiers came to Hibis. And yet, true to his word, the black blood on the sphinx is still fresh. Remember, <i>weret-hekau</i>, that we are as faithful as Sutekh even in death. We can bargain if you come as guests, but not as burglars.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We know the Red Land well. The western desert is the road to Duat, and we have wandered back and forth between the worlds with Sutekh's blessing. We can stand on your bow, chosen of Djehuty, and spear Apep when he swims close. If you know your destination, we can help you reach it and return to the world of life.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> After some preliminary negotiation, he offers these terms:<ul><li>Greater Request: Retainer 3 for the Term. Will assist in combat and act as secondary actor in travel rolls.</li> <li>2 Medial Costs: Someone in the caravan must offer blood freely at the end of each night, 2 Lethal damage. Each sorcerer must maintain a blessing on the Shadow for the Term.</li> <li>Medial Term: You must return to Hibis by Day 28, the end of the Aquarius cycle.</li> <li>Medial Forfeiture: If you do not meet the terms, the Shadow will capture one of the caravan for sufficient blood as they return to Hibis alone.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Instead of Poor Light, everyone in the tunnel has Blinded (-5 to rolls requiring vision, including Scrutiny/Revelation.)<br /> <br /> The Death/Matter mystery is Opacity 3. Poor vision penalties apply to Scrutiny/Revelation.<br /> <br /> With his x-success, Imhotep has an insight into negotiation: you could reduce the blood cost to 1 Lethal damage per night if one of you casts an appealing permanent spell on the Shadow before leaving for the Red Land, and a second permanent spell when you return.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:05:13-07:00","id":1063402,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 13/15</div><div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b>Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</div><br /> Shadow and death, this tunnel fairly reeked of miscreation. Yet was it not a miscreated star that now carved its bleeding path through his fate?<br /> <br /> The terms of the bargain are somewhat worrying when communicated though. Speaking to his companions, though he assumed anything he said would be overheard, and glancing down the tunnel from time to time he said, <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">It may be my magic would not be wanted given what it may bring forth. Should it be to this 'master' to judge, or shall we make our own best offer?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Activating Mage Sight: Fate, Space, and Time<br /> <br /> Assuming anything comes up going to try Revelation with Fate<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496931\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T13:32:40-07:00","id":1063441,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;Offer what you will, and we will weigh it against a feather. But a gravely poisoned blessing would be a violation of terms.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Time shows Khvarenah what is about to happen. If he keeps his Sight open, he can catch any tricks or surprise attacks a moment before they happen.<br /> <br /> Space gives him an idea of the dimensions of this place, despite the darkness. This low tunnel is about 20 yards long, and opens up into a wide, deep square chamber directly beneath the holy sanctuary of the temple proper.<br /> <br /> The &quot;heavy&quot; carvings that Imhotep observed are visible under Fate as well, but only on the walls of the square chamber ahead. Some faded boon animates them, like a web of lines drawn with chalk that has nearly eroded with time and neglect. The blessing is magic, resembling the Ruling practice of Fate, but not the kind that sorcerers like you practice. It has been here for <i>centuries</i>, since the Hibis temple was constructed, surely. The only thing close to a maker's signature is the vague fluttering suggestion of a golden falcon, the details long since lost to history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T14:03:06-07:00","id":1063482,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 13/15</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b>Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</div> <br /> <br /> Khvarenha considered for a moment.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Casting Momentary Flux to know what offers I could make would be beneficial<br /> Instant, Self, Standard Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency<br /> Reach: 1 free, 0 over<br /> Factors: Potency (primary) -0 (0 free steps), Duration -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: Shadowname +2 = 6<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 5 + Arche 1 + Yantras 2 - Penalties 0 = 8. Casting roll.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496936\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> If it will take more than one spell I will edit them in here to avoid multiposting.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T15:24:03-07:00","id":1063570,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired (Negotiations)| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><br /> Ever since they had entered the tunnels Unbound felt exposed,as if the darkness was full of eyes and intelligence on its own. He hoped he could even the odds at least a little, so he opened heimself to the realms of Mind, Space and Spirit.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Activating Mage Sight for the aforementioned Arcana<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He also didn't like the offer made by thestranger. That is a lot of blood, and he'd rather not have some undead monster sucking it from his (or anyone else's) neck. To grease the negotiation he pierced the man's brain for some personal details, hoping this will help push the right buttons. Aware that these... things are listening to them he crushed some dried herbs in his hand and made a circle out of them, inside of which it'd be possible for the group to talk without audible words.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How do you like it? It's called &lt;&lt;telepathy&gt;&gt;.&quot; </span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496950\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Know Nature on the Shadow<br /> Instant, Sensory, Standard Duration, Standard Scale, Standard Potency <br /> Reach: 3 free, 0 over (+1 to reveal Aspirations and Obsessions)<br /> Factors: Duration -0, Potency (primary) -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 = 10 Casting roll.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496951\" target=\"_blank\">Casting</a> Telepathy on the group<br /> Ritual, Touch, Advanced Duration (1 scene), Standard Scale, Standard Potency <br /> Reach: 2 free, 0 over (+1 to make it a three-way conversation) <br /> Factors: Duration -0, Potency (primary) -0, Scale -0<br /> Yantras: High Speech +2, Order Tool +1, Sacrament +1 = 4<br /> Nemesis: 0 from Reach, 0 from other sources, -0 from Mana/Tool.<br /> Spellcasting: Gnosis 3 + Arche 3 + Yantras 4 - Penalties 4 = 6 Casting roll.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:57:12-07:00","id":1063656,"title":"","content":"<b>Khvarenah</b> peers into the immediate future. Offering these dark creatures a Time working in place of a longer blessing (from him) would lead to good things. Of course, it's anyone's guess whether they would like the results. People have complicated relationships with diviners.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbound</b> opens his true eyes. Cruelty lurks in his Mind's eye, a mote behind his brow, chastised for now. He can't see the whole area clearly, but the only waking mind he senses besides the three sorcerers is the lone Shadow, which is mere inches away. Nothing else, not even dreamers.<br /> <br /> With Space, he sees the same information Khvarenah saw.<br /> <br /> With Spirit, he sees that the tunnel is Resonant with darkness itself in a way that mundane shadowy places are not. It doesn't look like any spirits have come from their hidden places, though.<br /> <br /> He draws a circle of sage. The Shadow speaks. <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;Why do you ward yourself, Greek? Do you think we cannot see you in the dark? Why do you come through our door and insult our hospitality? Guests have nothing to fear from us, only thieves.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> His flowing mind does not cross the circle. And hearing his voice is enough to sense and read his psyche.<br /> <br /> He thirsts. Pervading everything else, you feel a hunger deeper than anything you've ever felt, even the drive for ever-greater Gnosis. All his thoughts and actions are ultimately driven by bloodthirst, even if it's delayed. His reason is enslaved to his appetite. He <i>must</i> feed.<br /> <br /> The Shadow isn't good with people (Social tertiary, 6 dots), but he thinks deeply (Mental primary, 9 dots). He is <b>Cautious</b> to a fault, but prone to <b>Zealous</b> outbursts for his gods and masters.<br /> <br /> He is dearly devoted to his master. He has been in <i>henet</i> for years now, far too long. He urgently seeks a way to lift the mysterious curse laid on his master.<br /> <br /> He has heard rumors of the <i>sha,</i> beast of his patron god Sutekh/Set, seen in the desert lately. He considers it a sign and wants one brought back to lift the curse. In pursuit of this, he has mesmerized the priest Mitry to acquire one from a traveler.<br /> <br /> Finally, he wants to hunt and kill some creature that bedevils him. Visions of a shadowy bird with a golden beak and eyes, something like the <i>strigoi</i> of Greek legend. Maybe Alexander's armies brought something with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:54:06-07:00","id":1063683,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 13/15</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b>Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\">I beg your pardon for my ignorance, but it seems to me that this place and your master are most ancient. It seems the way of things that much is often buried by the ever flowing sand of time. Is there any such thing you or your master have lost which you dearly seek to regain? I do not say that I can, but depending on the nature of such things I might be able to render assistance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><i>I may have something that is worth more than blood and sorcery to them, but the reaction may be </i>excited<i>. I will make the offer if you are ready for what might come.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Manipulation 2 + Empathy 3 - 2 = 3<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/497057\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a><br /> Resolving steadfast</div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-17-2017, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T13:28:47-07:00","id":1064010,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain, -1 Dex till dawn day 4| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 6/15</div> <br /> <br /> Imhotep ponders.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\"><i>I'm not yet skilled enough to close wounds and replenish lost blood with sorcery, but I can make our bodies recover from wounds faster.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><i>I may have something that is worth more than blood and sorcery to them, but the reaction may be </i>excited<i>. I will make the offer if you are ready for what might come.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\"><i>What is it?</i></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Recognizing the meaning of henet in vampiric context: Int 3 + Academics 2 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/497207\" target=\"_blank\">5d10h8</a><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/497207\" target=\"_blank\">: <b>2</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:40:58-07:00","id":1064171,"title":"","content":"<b>Imhotep</b> recalls that <i>henet</i> refers to the mouth of the pelican, ferrying the dead safely to the afterlife. The undead do not sleep, they die, sometimes for months or years on end when they starve. But they always return, eventually, when fed blood again. They use <i>henet</i> to refer to this temporary death. This Shadow seems unusually worried, by <b>Unbound</b>'s reading, like there's something abnormal about this time.<br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah</b> manages to stir the Shadow's dead heart. Blessing his Fate probably helped. The boy speaks slowly and carefully, wherever he's lurking:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;The master fell into <i>henet</i> when the Greeks came to Hibis. Among their soldiers were men who could see the blood that mortals ignore. Tomb robbers. They plundered the temple and stole our reliquary, even the Scroll, before we drove them off. Even the master was laid low in the fighting. Since that night, the master will not wake. If we recovered the Scroll of Going Forth By Night, perhaps Lord Sutekh could be persuaded to lift his curse.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-19-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T03:02:38-07:00","id":1065154,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (2/3):</b> Know the Shadows, Shadow Crafting | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 6/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> Listening to the conversation he decides that this is getting them nowhere fast and he jumps down into the Tunnel. He thinks of a spell that will allow him to know there everything is in the darkness. Forming the Imago in his mind he thinks of the shadows outlining everything in the area the shadows are thick and where there is an absence of shadow there must be something their. As the Spell takes effect He expends the Inspired Condition that is upon him from Fate and pushes the spell to exceptional heights. He can see everyone and everything in the tunnels and all the rooms attached to the tunnels.<br /> <br /> Knowing where everyone is he now senses the Shadow that stands between them and their goal. Once again he calls upon the imago, this time it is a spell that he knows well. He imagines the shadows solidifying and encasing his subject. As the spell finishes the Shadow is encased in shadows, covering every inch of the Shadow Creature from head to toe in solid air tight shadow. Controlling the thickness around the head to be thinner than the rest so that the creature can still hear me, it will be muffled but he can still hear. Strife will join his companions in the circle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;I believe that I have <span style=\"font-size:12px\">neutralized</span> the Creature for now but we must hurry before the Priests finish their chanting.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Creative Thaumaturgy</b></span><br /> <b>Know the Shadows (Death \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Investigation, Occult, Subterfuge.<br /> The shadows belong to the Death mage and with this spell you cannot hide within them. The subject of this spell can sense with clarity anything that touches the shadows within an area. By sensing the absence of shadow he knows where everything is. This will remove the effects of the Low Light Condition from the subject. The area is centered on the subject and moves with him as he walks. Subtract the potency from stealth attempts make to hide in the shadows, and if someone is actively trying to hide in the shadows they can Withstand using Resolve. Anything moving through the area of effect faster than a walk just leaves a streak through the shadows.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> With this reach the subject knows the physical dimension of anything in the spells area, as the shadows cling to the object outlining every curve, crease, fold.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Actions</span></b><br /> <b>Rote/Praxis/Improvised Imago:</b> Know the Shadows (Death \u2022)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 3 (Arcane) +1 (Yantras) = 7 dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 3, Reaches used: 3 (1 to move to instant casting, 1 to change spell to Advanced Duration , 1 to change spell to Advanced Scale.)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Mace +1)<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/497915\" target=\"_blank\">Know the Shadows</a>: <u>7d10h8</u> <b>4</b>: Success, use Inspired Condition to make it an Exceptional Success removing withstand.<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Week (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Scale:</b> Large house or building<br /> <b>Range:</b> Self<br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Withstand Trait</b>: None<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 1 Turn.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Outline everything that is touched by shadows to get the outline of the tunnels and those in the tunnels.<br /> <br /> <b>Rote:</b> Shadow Crafting (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) + 3 (Arcane) +1 (Yantras) +3 (Willpower) +X (+1 /extra casting time interval) = XX dice pool.<br /> <b>Reaches:</b> Free Reaches: 3, Reaches used: X (1 to move to instant casting, 1 to change spell to Advanced Duration, 1 to change spell to Sensory.)<br /> <b>Yantras used:</b> (Mace +1)<br /> <br /> <b>Results:</b> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/497916\" target=\"_blank\">Shadow Crafting</a>: <u>7d10h8</u> <b>2</b>: Success<br /> <br /> <b>Ending Spell Factors:</b><br /> <b>Potency:</b> 1<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Week (<i>Primary</i>)<br /> <b>Scale:</b> 1 person<br /> <b>Range:</b> Sensory<br /> <b>Hekau Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Willpower Cost:</b> 0<br /> <b>Withstand Trait</b>: None, If it is ruled that there is a withstand associated with using the spell as attack then I will use the Charmed condition to turn this into an Exceptional Success to remove withstand.<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> 1 turn.<br /> <b>Desired Effect:</b> Turn the shadows that surround the Vampire into a solid skin tight shell covering his entire body encasing him in the Hardened shadows. Think of Hon Solo encased in the Carbonite.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-20-2017, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T08:29:06-07:00","id":1065251,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired (Negotiations)| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12<br /> </div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (All of this assumes that nothing interrupts Strife's plan)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the all-consuming darkness of the tombs, Strife's footsteps can be heard more clearly, but his surprise entrance made some impression on Unbound nonetheless. Assuming from the sudden bursts of magic that the Egyptian scribe attacked the Shadow creature, he is less than pleased.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;What in the BLAZES of Tartarus was that, exactly? I mean, as much as I appreciate silencing this sneaky bastard, now we have to destroy all of them. I don't think they'll let it slide, and from what we've seen they are a wicked and vengeful lot.&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> Not waiting for the answer he unsheathes his sword, making careful steps to be ready to strike at any moment. He is looking for anything that could serve as a makeshift torch or other source of light. If he finds it and manages to ignite it (such as with a flint) he will look around the chambers to find anything that could either be of help in the journey or might contain some knowledge on these strange creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:36:32-07:00","id":1065400,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain, -1 Dex till dawn day 4| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 6/15</div> <br /> <br /> Feeling sorcery flashing on his periphery, Imhotep opens his Sight again.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\">&quot;What? Stop!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He disrupts the Hekau swirls surrounding Strife (or at least, attempts to).<br /> <hr /><br /> Opening Sight to all ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> Countering Shadow Crafting, spending 1 Hekau to attempt and 1 Willpower: Gnosis 2 + Death 2 + WP 3 = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498043\" target=\"_blank\">7d10h8: <b>4</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 03-20-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T14:02:06-07:00","id":1065418,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (1/3):</b> Know the Shadows.| <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 9/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Speaking aloud <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;This is not the one you need to be negotiating with he is the lowest of the shadows. He is put her to befuddle the weak. If he will not take us to the one that can deal then he will be removed from the road as any droppings should be. You sit here treating his as your better when the priest near the end of their prays. &quot;</b></span> speaking with telepathy &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">you have one more chance to get him to deal or move aside.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Still looking around with his Know the shadows spell, he will pinpoint the rest of the Vampires in the lower complex.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498044\" target=\"_blank\">Clash of Wills</a>: <u>9d10h8</u> <b>2</b> his spell was blocked. spent 1 willpower on the Clash of Wills. Since you cancelled the spell before I cast it I didn't spend the charmed condition to bless the spell.<br /> <br /> The spell has an area of a large building it should cover the underground area, or most of it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-20-2017, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T22:53:28-07:00","id":1066128,"title":"","content":"<b>Strife </b>descends down into the tunnel and opens his eyes to the shadows. He does this so well, in fact, that he recovers 1 Mana. He then attempts to bind the Shadow-creature in its own dark aura, only to be countered successfully by <b>Imhotep.</b><br /> <br /> Strife sees the subtleties of the shadows obscuring the hidden chamber. The narrow brick tunnel is lined with notches and carved signs that seem to have ritual significance. At the end of the tunnel is a low square room with more elaborate carvings on the solid stone walls. There may be painted details and colors that the shadows still obscure. Strife recognizes on the far end of the wall a carved stone mural depicting the same scene that he meditated before in the temple proper: Set, standing proud on the solar barge of Ra, spearing the serpent Apophis to protect his lord. There are also several clay jars mounted on little altars, a scroll repository set into the wall, and heavy wooden chests for storage.<br /> <br /> At the center of the low room, some 30 yards away from you down the narrow tunnel, is a raised altar (or sarcophagus?) surrounded by heavy curtains. Perhaps the master sleeps here. There are three unmarked stone sarcophagi on the packed earth floor, flanking the central curtained one.<br /> <br /> Closer to the group, Strife feels that the boy Shadow is clinging to the ceiling behind them, wearing the darkness like a cloak and mask. He seethes:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;Enough of this. Terms have been offered. Will you do business, or shall we withdraw our hospitality?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Accept/Decline the terms originally presented? Or present an alternative? The Shadow is getting antsy.<br /> <br /> Strife can roll Wits+Crafts (Architecture) to assess the significance of this room if he likes, this is in his area of expertise.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T02:11:38-07:00","id":1066191,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (1/3):</b> Know the Shadows | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 10/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">In the telepathy he says this &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Offer him our assistance in finding the scroll and reliquary that he needs to raise the master and tell him that we can see if we can aid the master before we leave, I will not freely offer the blood of me of my wife to this shadow, or any member of the Caravan for that matter.&quot; </i></span></span><br /> <br /> Strife has his hand on his weapon as he looks up at the boy smiling <span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>&quot;I am a master of the darkness boy. You can not hide from me within. This substance that you play with is but a parlor trick.&quot;</b></span></span></span>. He continues to look around the space under the temple recognizing the layout of the chamber beyond.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498428\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Craft</a>: <u>5d10h8</u> <b>2</b> = Success, I have succeeded in knowing something of the significance of this space.<br /> <br /> BTW I was looking at the posts since day 3 and this scene began and I spent the Inspired during this scene but I do not see where you counted it in our total for arcane Beats. This was my first one this scene.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-24-2017, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:56:08-07:00","id":1066534,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Active (Death, Life, Matter) | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain, -1 Dex till dawn day 4| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 3/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 8/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 6/15</div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\"><i>I can offer him my blood, I can accelarate my recovery so it won't cause a problem. If we offer finding the scroll in addition to blood, we could ask him to tell us everything he knows about his master.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T23:30:14-07:00","id":1066718,"title":"","content":"<b>Strife </b>picks up on some of the details from his architectural training. Kemet had been under Persian rule for some 2 centuries before Alexander drove them out a few years ago, and the temple and town of Hibis were constructed early in this Persian period. What's strange is that the low chamber ahead of you matches the architectural style of a much earlier era, as far back as the New Kingdom of one thousand years ago. The design of this place is quite unlike the rest of the Hibis temple above it. It suggests that this place came first, and the temple was built later.<br /> <br /> Also notable is the system of regular notches and designs carved into the stone walls. They are cracked and eroded, remains of a bygone era. He's heard of hidden chambers with patterns like this before in especially ancient temples and guildhalls, places with a subtle but potent <i>Sekhem</i> that eludes Awakened senses. The more senior Weret-Hekau of Abydos, City of Tombs, know the most about these hidden chambers. All Strife knows for sure is that they are highly dangerous and have a way of attracting monsters and other unworthies. No wonder the Greek tomb-robbers broke in.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think you're right- I'll get caught up on the A-Beats and bookkeeping stuff later.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:28:50-07:00","id":1066941,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Khvarenah: <span style=\"color:#00008B\">Wandering Chaldean Astrologer</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed, Inspired, Illuminated, Star-Crossed, Steadfast| <b>Spells:</b> Exceptional Luck, Shifting the Odds<br /> <span style=\"color:#00008B\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 12/15</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Gear:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Clay Tablet [academics] (+2), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate &amp; Space Sacraments</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> The Persian was angry. He had risked miscreation to turn aside the new thorns growing like weeds from Strife and cut off the futures they portended. Worse, he had failed and another did what should have been his task.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00008B\">Here is my counteroffer. I will recover this scroll for you. In exchange, you will guide us to the hand, not interfere with what we do there, and permit us to discuss a matter of importance with your master. If blood is absolutely necessary for you there are options we are willing to consider. Should you value the remainder of your reliquary I will hear offers on your part for their retrieval as well.<br /> <br /> If you should happen to have a piece of the place of the hand or some deep attachment to it, that might be sufficient for our purposes, but I make no promises until I know if it is worth anything to us.<br /> <br /> How does this sound to you?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Khvarenah had not felt this vulnerable since he fled Iskander. Though he had never worn armor, for years he had clothed himself in ever thicker layers of good fortune and lucky chance. Now Strife put them all at risk, when he was the one who stood before the miscreated wretch and stood to be the first to fall to its knives. How dare he! How dare he treat Khvarenah as scenery for his grand performance, swooping in as if he were some god or hero-king.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#00008B\">Never do that again. If you had misjudged or failed we might have died or suffered great harm. Your vanity and frustration are not worth our safety.Merely to prevent the damage you did from being worse has cost us already, and now you compound it with braggadocio! Unless you have power to dictate terms entire, and you do not because we do not know all of what we need or they have, such threats as that raise walls against our arguments and make the task harder than it already was.</span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:12:12-07:00","id":1067339,"title":"","content":"Now we're gettin' somewhere. The Shadow replies:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">&quot;The Scroll of Going Forth by Night is most precious. We will not discuss the remainder.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The blood cannot be denied. No contract or oath can overcome our Great Oath to Sutekh: blood for life. Payment for service. But you are cunning men. Help us hunt in the Red Land, and we need not drink of you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We will guide you truly and let you do as you will. The master may know of the Hand of U'mat, but he does not speak while in <i>henet</i>. If you have a way of speaking to him, you may try. But anyone who would enter the inner chamber must honor our hospitality by drinking the black wine.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The voice of Cruelty whispers in Unbound's ear: <i>&quot;</i><i><span style=\"color:#8B4513\">the fat old tick isn't dead. he's dreaming.&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Shadow suggests modified terms. Accept/Decline?<ul><li>Greater Request: Retainer 3 for the Term. Will assist in combat and act as secondary actor in travel rolls. An audience with the master will be granted, to the extent possible.</li> <li>2 Medial Costs: Someone (Imhotep?) must assist with a hunting roll each night to feed on animals, and/or offer their own blood on a failure. Khvarenah will recover the Scroll.</li> <li>Medial Term: You must return to Hibis and recover the Scroll by Day 28. The order doesn't matter, but they both need to happen.</li> <li>Medial Forfeiture: If you do not meet the terms, the Shadows will tell their network throughout Kemet that you are enemies and oathbreakers.</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:59:42-07:00","id":1067457,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Strife: <span style=\"color:darkred\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Death Scribe</a> of Anpu - The Hand of Death \u2013 His Lords Warrior</span></b><br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros | <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra | <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Spells Controlled (1/3):</b> Know the Shadows | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Informed.<br /> <b>Spells Cast On Him:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Health: L</b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 5/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 10/12 (3)<br /> <br /> <b>Gear:</b> Crafting Gear (+2), Mace (Dedicated Magic Tool), 4 Javelins (In back sheath), Medical Supplies<br /> Death Sacraments, Fate Sacraments.</div> <hr /><br /> Thinking to the rest of the group '<i><span style=\"color:#800080\">The terms now seem acceptable to me and as long as the rest of you find them acceptable we can rap this up. Neither death nor harm would have happened as the spell I was casting would have hardened the very shadows around him and he would not have been able to move, the safety of the group is always foremost on my mind. The negotiations were happening to slowly we have more to worry about than this boy. My actions did not harm the negotiations, The term remained unchanged until the offer to find the scroll, which I suggested, you taking on that task as your task was your Idea and not forced upon you by the situation. And what you call Braggadocio it tactics in negotiations as you let them know that they do not hold all of the power at the table. So do not presume to be my better and order me as you would a servant.</span></i>'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:43:44-07:00","id":1067992,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Unbound: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Greek Binder of Daevas</span></b><br /> <b>Mage Sight:</b> Peripheral | <b>Conditions:</b> Informed, Inspired (Negotiations)| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>Health: </b>OOOOOOO</span> | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Mana:</b> 9/12 <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>Enough of this. He &quot;said&quot; to Khvarenah and Strife. We can argue all day *after* we leave the lair of a blood-drinking, shadow-commanding monster. For now, let's accept its terms and move on. I will keep an eye on him, and if he tries anything we'll see how immortal it is with a sword in its heart.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;Tell me, Shadow&quot;</b></span> he is trying to face the direction from which its voice was last heard <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>&quot;What this Scroll is actually used for? How does it look? Do you have any idea how did these &lt;&lt;robbers&gt;&gt; look, how did they find you or where they were headed? I will not force you to answer, but it might be wise if you want this artfiact returned.&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> You know anything useful about this creature? If yes, speak, if you don't do me a favor and shut up - he said to Cruelty</div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:30:42-07:00","id":1070765,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#40D080\">Imhotep</span>, scribe-physician of Anubis</b><br /> <b>Sorcerous Sight:</b> Active (Death, Life, Matter) | <b>Conditions:</b> Charmed, Steadfast(?), Team Player, Dead Certain, -1 Dex till dawn day 4| <b>Spells:</b> none<br /> <b>Health:</b> OOOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 3/6 | <b>Hekau:</b> 8/11 (2)<br /> <b>Gear:</b> Writing utensils [Academics, Enigmas] (+1), Matter &amp; Life Sacraments<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Urbi</span>, emissary of Anubis (???)</b><br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Familiar, Resonant, Open, Fettered<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Health:</b> OOOOOO | <b>Willpower:</b> 8/8 | <b>Essence:</b> 6/15</div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#40D080\"><i>Khvarenah, do you feel we can do this within a month? If so, we can accept.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}